INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('seeing-is-believing-how-guest-facing-displays-build-trust-drive-up-tips-aug-31', 'Boost Tips & Trust: How Guest Facing Displays Engage Diners', 'In the fast-changing world of restaurants, the best way to be always ahead of the rest is to ensure that innovation plays a key role in raising the customer experience. While great food and excellent service are key,...', '[{"type":"p","text":"In the fast-changing world of restaurants, the best way to be always ahead of the rest is to ensure that innovation plays a key role in raising the customer experience. While great food and excellent service are key, there is a quiet savior who works behind the scenes in legitimizing your business: the guest facing display."},{"type":"p","text":"After all, the digital marvels are far superior to the simple purpose of showing menus. These will become the dynamic way to hopefully communicate trust, transparency, and even tips! Research by QSR Magazine indicates that display systems facing customers can reduce wait times by up to 40%. This improvement in service speed leads to higher customer turnover and satisfactionLet''s delve into the gains of guest facing displays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Gain Trust with Transparency"},{"type":"p","text":"The static menu age and the shadow of doubt over pricing are laid to rest because the guest facing display will allow you to show the offerings with attractive visuals. Here''s how that moves the needle on trust:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Real-time Updates"},{"type":"p","text":"Prices fluctuate, and specials often change daily. Guest facing displays ensure that your menu is consistently updated with the latest information so your patrons don''t get confused and frustrated."},{"type":"h2","text":"Detailed Descriptions"},{"type":"p","text":"Go beyond just the name of a dish. Guest facing displays offer plenty of room for promoting fresh ingredients, cooking methods, and dietary considerations. This can help the consumer make the right choice with confidence and willfully put their trust or savings in your hands."},{"type":"h2","text":"Promotional Clarity"},{"type":"p","text":"Offers and combos can be well displayed with uttermost clarity on guest facing displays, therefore being aware of all of the offers and potential value that can occur. Transparency creates trust and the feeling of a partnership with your institution."},{"type":"h2","text":"Engaging Customers and Increasing Tips"},{"type":"p","text":"Guest facing displays are more than informative; they engage your customers. Here''s how they subtly suggest and persuade your customer to leave a nice, big tip:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Visual Storytelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Forget the overload of words. Display with high-quality images and short videos that showcase your signature dishes in their full, tasty splendor. The appetizing visuals will whet the appetite and increase cravings, creating a perfect dining experience that your customers wouldn''t mind appreciating with a gratuity."},{"type":"h2","text":"Highlighting Staff Recommendations"},{"type":"p","text":"Displays for customers can also help in establishing staff recommendations and guiding customers to what your staff enjoys most. This personal touch is an amazing point to be proud of and a subtle insinuation to the customer to rely on the team''s intuition. Customers who feel well-guided will more frequently show their gratitude through better tips."},{"type":"h2","text":"Promoting Tipping Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Let''s be honest: most often, the customer is taken aback when you provide them with a tip prompt. With guest facing displays that can show multiple payment options, including contactless ones, you essentially imply a tip to the customer. This makes the process much more seamless, and the customers that much more guilt-free, and unafraid of emerging awkwardness."},{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond Tips: The Power of Upselling"},{"type":"p","text":"While it is one of the key features, guest facing displays do more than act as a digital tip jar. Without being pushy, you can easily upsell:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Model Add-on Symbols"},{"type":"p","text":"Appetizers, desserts, and specialty drinks all can be displayed with appetizing photographs and descriptions. In this way, you provide your customer with a rather unsubtle nudge that they deserve one more treat, which further raises the value of their average order."},{"type":"h2","text":"Promote Happy Hour Offers"},{"type":"p","text":"Use the digital signage guest facing displays to advertise your happy hour. Attract customers to stick around and drink up with an awesome deal."},{"type":"h2","text":"Promote Local Delicacies"},{"type":"p","text":"Encourage local favorites or in-season delicacies that give your customers a new experience with each visit."},{"type":"p","text":"Remember, the key to success with guest facing displays is keeping them fresh dynamic, and up-to-date:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep Content Fresh"},{"type":"p","text":"Swap out visuals, descriptions, and promotional offers often to make it interesting for customers who might visit time and time again."},{"type":"h2","text":"Dayparting"},{"type":"p","text":"Showcase breakfast items in the morning? Display happy-hour apps at night."},{"type":"h2","text":"Incorporate interactive features."},{"type":"p","text":"Interactive displays allow customers to customize their orders or learn more about menu items for deeper interest and greater satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Call to Action: Unleash the Power of Guest Facing Displays"},{"type":"p","text":"In a competitive landscape, every edge counts. Guest facing displays are not just screens; they are powerful tools for shifting trust, engaging diners, and, most importantly, growing tips and revenue in the digital age. Step back and watch your restaurant flourish in the magic of seeing it happen."},{"type":"p","text":"Unlock the potential of guest facing displays: Take a look at displays that we have listed on eatOS. Our displays seamlessly blend with the existing systems in your restaurant making it easier to adapt. Build the future of your restaurant with us today."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_bdc9f5d10afc4815803b53801fc1629d~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Insights', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-07-10', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('pouring-profits-not-money-down-the-drain-cost-effective-point-of-sale-solutions-for-bars-restaur', '''Boost Profits with Point of Sale Solutions for Bars & Restaurants''', 'A successful bar or restaurant needs to find the delicate balance between cost control, excellent customer service, and operational consistency. One such factor that can either work for your venture''s success or against...', '[{"type":"p","text":"A successful bar or restaurant needs to find the delicate balance between cost control, excellent customer service, and operational consistency. One such factor that can either work for your venture''s success or against it is the point of sale (POS) system you adopt. A good bar restaurant point-of-sale system optimizes operations, increases customer satisfaction, and finally lets you pour profits rather than money down the drain. In this article, we look at some affordable point-of-sale solutions that are targeted at bars and restaurants and discuss how such systems can improve your business."},{"type":"h2","text":"Why a Bar Restaurant''s point of sale System Is So Vital?"},{"type":"h2","text":"Improving Efficiency and Speed"},{"type":"p","text":"The business line might be heavy in the lively atmosphere of a bar or restaurant. A strong restaurant point-of-sale system increases the speed of processing different orders, and hence fewer delays lead to faster delivery to customers. These systems allow the correct information to be relayed to the kitchen and bar staff quickly as they easily integrate with all other operational tools."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reducing Errors and Waste"},{"type":"p","text":"Human error is inevitable, but a good point-of-sale system goes a long way in materially minimizing errors. Point of Sale systems allow for real-time inventory tracking and low-stock alerts, enabling businesses to optimize ordering and minimize stockouts. Studies suggest a 20% reduction in inventory shrinkage with point-of-sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Features like order accuracy checks and real-time management of inventory can help significantly avoid mistakes that might happen in the order-taking process, say in the kitchen and on the way to the client''s table. Improved customer satisfaction means reduced waste in terms of wrongly prepared orders, monetary waste to the business is cut in the form of food and beverages that would have been thrown away."},{"type":"h2","text":"Improving Customer Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"A well-implemented point-of-sale system will enhance the customer experience. Equipped with table management, split billing, and integration with loyalty programs, you are all set to provide excellent and personalized dining experiences to your customers. They will appreciate the convenience and efficiency of these, and these might draw them magnetically back into your restaurant for further comments and reviews."},{"type":"h2","text":"Cloud point of sale Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Cloud-based point-of-sale solutions have great benefits for not only retailers but also bars and restaurants. These systems have low upfront costs and will scale with your business as it grows. On a cloud-based system, you can access data from anywhere, whenever a need arises for better management of different locations or remote monitoring of performance. In addition, the provider takes care of updates and maintenance, reducing IT costs and downtime."},{"type":"h2","text":"Mobile Point of Sale Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"First and foremost, mobile point-of-sale systems are developed to meet the standards of today. A mobile point of sale is perfect for a bar or restaurant that seeks to optimize space and increase the speed of service. Such systems allow servers to take an order and process payment right at the table with the help of a tablet or smartphone. This not only speeds up service but also increases customer experience by reducing queue times. Many mobile point-of-sale systems are more cost-optimized than the traditional fixed terminal and can easily be expanded depending on the business needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Open-Source point of sale Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Open-source point-of-sale systems are the best for an ultra-tech-savvy restaurateur. High flexibility in the software allows users to integrate many functions and features if need be. While open-source systems result in heightened technical demands for setup and maintenance, they provide the flexibility to design an ideal point-of-sale solution for your business without the high costs tagged onto proprietary software solutions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Integrated Payment Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"An integrated payment process in your point-of-sale system can save you hundreds of dollars a month in transaction fees, streamline the accounting process, and make payment an easy process. Integrated systems help to reduce errors and assure the user of their secure transactions with processing done expediently. Look for a point-of-sale provider who offers competitive rates and free equipment with transparent pricing to make sure you save as much as possible."},{"type":"h2","text":"Key Features of a Bar Restaurant point of sale System"},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Most importantly, effective inventory management is vital in controlling the cost and minimizing waste. An effective point-of-sale system indeed provides real-time tracking of your inventory and automatic alerts regarding stock situations, coupled with detailed reports to help you stay on top of your inventory and make sure you order right without overordering."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reporting and Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Comprehensive analytics in sales and reporting enables a business to make informed decisions and consequently turn around its sales. Seek a point of sale that has extremely detailed reports on sales, customer insights, and performance. These analytics will help identify trends, understand customer preferences, and optimize your menu and price strategies."},{"type":"h2","text":"Staff Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Effectively managing staff brings the best out of them. Good point-of-sale software will allow you to manage employees using their hours, and shifts, and tracking performance to ensure that you have the right human resources during a peak period and not be overstaffed in off-peak periods."},{"type":"h2","text":"Customer Relationship Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop good relationships with your customers. A point of sale with a CRM collects and analyzes the details of customers, tracks buying history, and enables a business to issue a loyalty program. It offers you a chance to do customer-tailored promotions and rewards, therefore helping you to build high customer loyalty to satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"The investment in an affordable bar restaurant point-of-sale, in the long run, will have a positive impact that eventually saves and grows your profits. A point-of-sale system will change your business capabilities, increasing efficiency while reducing errors and enhancing great customer service. Get a cloud-based, mobile, or open-source system suiting your business needs and budget."},{"type":"p","text":"Are you ready to pour in profits instead of your money going straight down the drain? Find the perfect bar restaurant point of sale for your business at eatOS now and start realizing the benefits of a streamlined operation and satisfied customers. Contact us now to learn more!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_56bff6b7df904fd5b856d822b81c9112~mv2.jpg', 'Inventory Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-07-06', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('savings-on-tap-pour-profits-into-your-restaurant-with-eatos-point-of-sale-aug-28', '''Efficient and Profitable: eatOS Point-of-Sale System for Sale''', 'Picture this: your restaurant running like a well-oiled money machine. Every penny managed, margins healthy, and overflowing glasses bring in more than just smiles. Sounds like a dream, doesn''t it? Well, a point-of-sale...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Picture this: your restaurant running like a well-oiled money machine. Every penny managed, margins healthy, and overflowing glasses bring in more than just smiles. Sounds like a dream, doesn''t it? Well, a point-of-sale system for sale is the dream, and it can become your reality."},{"type":"h2","text":"Stop the Money Drain: How eatOS Point of Sale Saves You Big"},{"type":"p","text":"Running a restaurant is a never-ending combat with expenses. Food costs, labor, rent, they all keep piling up. But what if your point of sale was an ally in the fight, not another leak to your resources? Here''s how eatOS point of sale gets you more cash flow:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Slash Processing Fees"},{"type":"p","text":"Bringing down the fees on credit card processing is like negotiating with a sour head chef. But eatOS point of sale brings together our industry clout to get the lowest possible fee, helping put back more of your profit on the table with every transaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management Made Easy"},{"type":"p","text":"Food waste remains a silent thief that gnaws away at profits, but with eatOS point of sale, your inventory is noticed in real-time, so you know what is moving and what is, for some reason, not. Turn those insights into smart ordering that reduces spoilage and quickly refills hot sellers, all resulting in satisfied customers who always get the dishes they crave."},{"type":"p","text":"Scheduling can be a logistical nightmare. eatOS point of sale analyzes sales data to help you establish data-driven schedules. Ensure you have the right staff on hand during peak hours and avoid unnecessary payroll expenses during slower periods."},{"type":"h2","text":"Faster Service, Lower Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Long lines and long waits are a disaster waiting to happen, right in the face of your customer and revenue loss. Studies show that point-of-sale systems can improve order processing times by up to 30%, leading to faster service and happier customers."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS utilizes a user-friendly interface for faster checkout processes, whether it''s staff using the device or customers for a smoother dining experience. Happy customers spend more, and that means a healthier bottom line."},{"type":"h2","text":"Interactive Dining and an Optimized Service Process"},{"type":"p","text":"While cost savings are the delicious appetizer, the real feast lies in the rich feature set of eatOS point of sale:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Cloud-Based Convenience"},{"type":"p","text":"Imagine running your restaurant from anywhere in the world, at any time. Say goodbye to the pain of clunky hardware with eatOS, and have full, safe, and easy access to your restaurant''s data. Menu updates, inventory control, and sales reporting could all be done in the palms of your hands."},{"type":"h2","text":"Easy Menu Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Edit your menu with ease, featuring seasonal promotions with succulent descriptions, and sort all your dishes into categories to help your guests find exactly what they are looking for. Choose a dynamic menu that is sure to leave your customer coming for more."},{"type":"h2","text":"Decision-Making Using Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Ditch the spreadsheets and unleash the power of insights! eatOS point of sale comes with in-depth reports about your business, sales trends, employee performance, and customer behavior. All this data can be used to make strategic decisions , from menu optimization to marketing strategies that will leverage the highest ROI."},{"type":"h2","text":"Real Savings, Real Results: Why eatOS Point of Sale is Different"},{"type":"p","text":"Why spend more time and money on a point of sale that can feel more like another expense than an investment in your restaurant''s future? Here are just a few reasons why:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Subscription-Based Model for Predictable Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"The other systems are expensive when bought upfront. eatOS point of sale is subscription-based, and you can budget your point of sale system costs with monthly expenses. It frees up the capital to be used in other areas."},{"type":"p","text":"Whether it''s a small bistro or a busy chain of restaurants, eatOS''s point of sale scales with your business. Our flexible plans assume you''ll only pay for intended features, adding functionalities with ease as your restaurant grows."},{"type":"h2","text":"Focus on what matters."},{"type":"p","text":"Managing a restaurant is a full-time job in itself. eatOS point-of-sale takes away the headaches of working with a point-of-sale system. Our interface is ultra-user-friendly, and we have second-to-none customer service to make it easy on the operator, so he can focus on his core competencies: making great food and creating unforgettable dining experiences for clients."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ready to Pour Profits Back into Your Restaurant?"},{"type":"p","text":"Get in the way of financial freedom, do not let any traditional point-of-sale system hold you back. Move to eatOS for a new level of efficiency, profitability, and customer joy. Get in touch for a demo now and see how eatOS'' point of sale can turn your restaurant into a cash-flowing success story."},{"type":"p","text":"Don''t wait! Take control of the future of your restaurant and start pouring profits with eatOS point of sale."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_ea8f838865964ce19de32e58d4b8b9f8~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-07-05', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-pros-and-cons-of-online-ordering-and-delivery-a-consumer-s-perspective-aug-27', 'Maximizing Online Ordering and Delivery: A Consumer''s Perspective', 'In the modern, dynamic world, ordering and delivery are progressively being added as part of the food business. From the ease and convenience of getting a meal by just taping a smartphone to the anticipation of getting...', '[{"type":"p","text":"In the modern, dynamic world, ordering and delivery are progressively being added as part of the food business. From the ease and convenience of getting a meal by just taping a smartphone to the anticipation of getting a meal right at the doorstep, it is no wonder at all as to why adopted the trend en masse. It thus affects restaurant owners or managers in knowing the consumer''s perspective about online ordering and delivery. In this article, we will take into consideration the pros and cons, from a customer''s point of view, of how a point of sale system for delivery business is efficient."},{"type":"h2","text":"Amazing Benefits of Point of Sale System for Delivery Business"},{"type":"p","text":"Studies show that point-of-sale software can lead to a significant decrease in order errors. One study found a reduction of up to 80%. This is due to features like order entry automation and digital displays, minimizing human error and ensuring order accuracy. Let us learn more advantages of this system:"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Maximum Convenience"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most significant advantages of online ordering and delivery for consumers is convenience. No more waiting in long lines or dealing with busy phone lines, customers can place orders from the comfort of their homes or offices."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. A World of Choices"},{"type":"p","text":"The range of choices provided by the online ordering platforms allows consumers to experience different cuisines and restaurants that they would otherwise have not tried. This large variety makes it quite easy for consumers to get what they want."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Saves Time"},{"type":"p","text":"For busy professionals, parents, and anyone with a hectic schedule, online ordering saves precious time. With just a few clicks, they can have a meal on the way, eliminating the need to cook or go out to eat."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Personalization and Customization"},{"type":"p","text":"Many ordering platforms offer the ability to modify orders according to preferences, such as modifying ingredients or selecting special diet choices. All of these add to personalization in dining."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Contactless Delivery Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Contactless delivery options became particularly favored because of the COVID-19 pandemic. Consumers appreciate added safety and extra convenience in food delivery without having to be in direct contact."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Downsides of Online Ordering and Delivery"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Delivery Fees and Minimum Order Requirements"},{"type":"p","text":"Delivery is convenient in many ways, although it can be expensive. The delivery fee, magnified with a minimum order requirement, brings the ultimate price to consumers, making it unaffordable for many."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Potential for Mistakes"},{"type":"p","text":"The technology age can''t eliminate mistakes in order. Wrong items, missing condiments, and perhaps even the wrong kind of customization will leave consumers frustrated and disappointed."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Quality Concerns"},{"type":"p","text":"Food quality during transit is not guaranteed. Cold or soggy food can kill someone''s appetite on arrival, among other dining experiences, and this will register as negative reviews and complaints from customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Long Wait Times"},{"type":"p","text":"The delivery wait times can be long. Customers can sometimes be hungry and finally end up waiting longer than they could have loved, which is a big minus."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Less Interaction"},{"type":"p","text":"Some feel that not interacting with the restaurant staff is a loss for the customer experience. Personal attachments, to being able to ask something or request something special, can make the experience pleasurable."},{"type":"h2","text":"How does a Point of Sale System for Delivery Business Help?"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Streamlined Order Management"},{"type":"p","text":"An earnest delivery point-of-sale system like eatOS can handle orders seamlessly, ensuring that the orders are processed correctly and concurrently forwarded to the kitchen. This lowers the error occurrence and gives rise to efficiency."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Real-time Tracking"},{"type":"p","text":"Most of the modern point-of-sale systems present a real-time order tracking feature that would aid the consumer in viewing the status of his delivery. Such type of transparency tends to heighten the user experience since the consumers are well-updated regarding food arrival timing."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Integrable Payment Solutions"},{"type":"p","text":"A good point-of-sale system integrates numerous payment options, hence making it easier for consumers to pay online. This may speed up the ordering process and lower the potential risks of potential problems concerning payment."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Customer Relationship Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Point-of-sale systems equipped with CRM store information on customers and their orders to enable personalized promotions and loyalty rewards. This may help satisfy the customer and result in repeated business."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Efficient Delivery Coordination"},{"type":"p","text":"For restaurants running their delivery, this is where a point of sale system comes in handy in managing the routes and schedules of the deliveries effectively. Orders go out on time, and food quality is preserved during transport."},{"type":"h2","text":"Tips to Improve Your Online Ordering and Delivery"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Use Good Packaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Good packaging is what will preserve your food during the trip. Quality packaging maintains your warm or cold food with no spills or breakage."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Multiple Options for Delivery"},{"type":"p","text":"Offer customers options such as standard, express, and contactless delivery according to their liking or where they live."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Have Clear Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Communication will largely go a long way in smoothening the delivery process. Give the customer an approximate time of delivery correctly, alert them about any deviations from this, and send order confirmations and receipts promptly."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Request for Feedback"},{"type":"p","text":"Ask for feedback from customers about the delivery experience. This will help point things out that need change and ensure that recurring issues have been resolved."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Promote Your Online Ordering Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Advertise online ordering and delivery on your social media, and website, and also do certain in-house promotions. Special promotions or discounts for first-time users will bring in many new customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion: Embrace the Future of Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"The stage of online ordering and delivery is jam-packed with challenges and, at the same time, provides plenty of opportunities. By knowing what''s in the consumer''s mind from all of these tools, ultimately what you have is turning these present weaknesses into strengths and creating advantages in your customers'' dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Take your restaurant''s online ordering and delivery to the next level with a top-grade point-of-sale system from eatOS that can help you achieve management perfected to the dot in the digital age. Make every dining experience stress-free, efficient, and enjoyable for your customers today! Book a demo with us today."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_ebd55aaa2f414ce8bc7cdfcbc3973f55~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-30', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('bar-restaurant-point-of-sale-features-what-you-need-to-know-aug-25', 'Essential Bar Restaurant Point of Sale System Features for Your Business', 'It''s not an easy task to run a bar or a restaurant. Right from managing the inventory to keeping the customers satisfied, the list of responsibilities seems to have no end. It is one tool that is going to make your life...', '[{"type":"p","text":"It''s not an easy task to run a bar or a restaurant. Right from managing the inventory to keeping the customers satisfied, the list of responsibilities seems to have no end. It is one tool that is going to make your life easy and make you completely free: a bar restaurant point of sale system. What key features should you look for? So let us deliberate on the most important features of a bar restaurant''s point of sale and how each one can revolutionize the way you do your business."},{"type":"h2","text":"Why Do You Need a Bar Restaurant Point of Sale System?"},{"type":"p","text":"But before getting into features, it''s important to know why a point-of-sale system for bar restaurants can be a game-changer. Such systems are specially tailored so that operations are more comfortable, more efficient, and managed in a customer-friendly way. Through the automation of tasks and the provision of valuable insights, a point-of-sale system will affect your bottom line."},{"type":"p","text":"Studies show that Point of Sale software can lead to a significant decrease in order errors by up to 80%. This applies to both food and drink orders, minimizing mistakes and customer frustration in bar restaurants."},{"type":"h2","text":"Key Features of a Bar Restaurant Point of Sale"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Stock Management"},{"type":"p","text":"An effective inventory control system benefits any bar or restaurant. A robust point-of-sale system can monitor inventory levels in real time, thus alerting you when stock is low or when there is a discrepancy. It does this quite effectively, thereby ensuring that you will not be depleted of significant products within your establishment, and it can help guard against theft and some forms of waste."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Sales Reporting and Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand your sales pattern; this is very important in running the business. A good point-of-sale system for a bar restaurant will furnish you with in-depth sales reports and embedded analytics. You could narrowly nail down the top-selling items, peak hours in business, and customer preferences, information, that would help in tailoring offerings and optimizing operations."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Employee Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Keeping staff schedules, the in and out time punches, and monitoring employee performance, are the biggest hassles. However having a point-of-sale system with employee management functionalities can ease this task: it will include managing hours worked, maintaining shifts, and sometimes even sales reports by employees to better manage your team."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Customer Relationship Management (CRM)"},{"type":"p","text":"Repeat business is only possible if you have built a strong relationship with customers. With CRM functionality in a point-of-sale system, you have features for storing customer information, tracking purchase history, and customizing promotions. This not only enhances the satisfaction but also boosts the loyalty of your customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Table Management"},{"type":"p","text":"For table-service-oriented restaurants, a watchful eye on efficient management is also definite at the tables. Point-of-sale systems for bars assist restaurants in managing reservations, monitoring table status, and seating arrangements to ensure guests a smooth dining experience and to be able to accommodate the maximum number of seated guests."},{"type":"h2","text":"6\\. Faster, More Accurate Transactions"},{"type":"p","text":"The speed and accuracy required in a busy bar or restaurant are incomparable. A dependable point of sale ensures quick yet accurate transactions, continuously reducing waiting time and cutting down on errors. This enhances customer service and helps maintain positive reputability."},{"type":"h2","text":"7\\. Mobile point of sale Capabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Mobile point-of-sale systems let staff members take orders and process payments from anywhere inside the dining area. This flexibility can help improve service efficiency and reduce the time customers spend waiting in line. It is particularly important if you have an outdoor seating area or just large overall dimensions of the place."},{"type":"h2","text":"8\\. Integration with Other Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"A versatile bar-restaurant point-of-sale system must integrate well with the tools you use, such as accounting software, online ordering platforms, and kitchen display systems. This comes in handy for the smooth flow of information and greatly saves time through the elimination of manual data entry, which reduces errors."},{"type":"h2","text":"Special Features to Look For"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Loyalty Programs"},{"type":"p","text":"Built-in loyalty programs can motivate repeat business by rewarding customers based on their continued patronage. Track points, reward, and understand the spending habits of your customers by using your point of sale so that you can further tailor your marketing campaigns to them."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Online Ordering and Delivery Integration"},{"type":"p","text":"In the current surge of online ordering and delivery, your point of sale needs to be integrated with these to guarantee a smooth procedure from order placement to delivery, hence increasing customer satisfaction and expanding reach in the process."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Advanced Security Features"},{"type":"p","text":"Top on the list is to protect your business, along with customer, data. Check for a point of sale with modern security features like transaction encryption, access control between users, and scheduled software updates to prevent cyber threats."},{"type":"h2","text":"Choose the right bar restaurant point of sale system"},{"type":"p","text":"There are many available options, and it cannot be easy to choose the right Point of Sale. Here is a set of guidelines to help you make the right decision."},{"type":"h2","text":"Be Aware of What You Need"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify your specific business needs and seek a point-of-sale system that will meet them. Consider the size of your operation, the number of staff, and the service style."},{"type":"h2","text":"Read Reviews and Get Recommendations"},{"type":"p","text":"Research different point-of-sale systems; read through reviews, and get referrals from other bar and restaurant owners about their experience with specific point-of-sale systems. This can give you great insight into how well certain systems perform and whether they are reliable."},{"type":"h2","text":"Take Advantage of Free Trials"},{"type":"p","text":"Most of the point-of-sale providers offer free trials or demonstrations. Take advantage of this to test the system at the ground level, meeting your needs."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider the importance of customer support: A reliable customer support system is quite essential, even when there are technical problems. There is a need to choose a provider who offers 24/7 support to help solve your problems whenever they occur."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion: Invest in the Success of Your Bar Restaurant"},{"type":"p","text":"A restaurant bar point-of-sale management system will do much more compared to a mere cash register: it is a complete package that can be used to ensure the smooth running of operations, enhance efficiency, and improve the customer experience, among others. You can raise your bar or restaurant to the next level with the correct features."},{"type":"p","text":"Ready to transform your bar or restaurant? Join us at eatOS. Explore our top-rated bar restaurant point-of-sale systems today and find the perfect fit for your business. Book a demo with us today. Your journey to improved efficiency and customer satisfaction starts now!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_48c4e6420bba405ea3a8dbe6d5413d7c~mv2.jpg', 'Inventory Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-29', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('optimizing-customer-engagement-and-satisfaction-with-guest-facing-displays-aug-24', 'Unlocking Restaurant Success: The Power of Guest Facing Displays', 'In the fast-moving environment of restaurants, every transaction with a customer matters. You want them to have a most positive, unforgettable experience from the time they step through your door until they depart. This...', '[{"type":"p","text":"In the fast-moving environment of restaurants, every transaction with a customer matters. You want them to have a most positive, unforgettable experience from the time they step through your door until they depart. This brings us to the guest facing display, very underappreciated for its potential to elevate an extra layer of a customer''s engagement and satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"These digital displays, whether at the counter or throughout your restaurant, have the potential to be much more than just glorified price lists. If you capitalize on their potential, they can become silent salespeople, brand ambassadors, and overall experience enhancers."},{"type":"h2","text":"How Guest Facing Displays Can Supercharge Your Restaurant?"},{"type":"p","text":"Displays facing customers have numerous advantages that will certainly create a satisfied clientele and are the key to business success. Studies suggest that CFDs with order confirmation can lead to a 5% decrease in order errors. This is because customers can verify their order details on the screen, reducing the likelihood of mistakes. Let us look in detail now how they have magic to assist your restaurant:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Transparency and Ease of Gain in Trust"},{"type":"p","text":"No order confusion, no billing surprises. Customers can see, in real-time, how their order details are being acquired in displays facing customers: which items were selected, what customizations were made, and the final price. This transparency tends to increase trust among people and reduces the need for clarification, thereby having a streamlined ordering process."},{"type":"h2","text":"Less Waiting Time, Higher Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"Nothing gets customers off on the wrong foot like long lines and delays. Displays facing customers can make a big difference in the perception of wait time, engaging them with menu items and promotions, and even offering ordering at the screen to further speed up service."},{"type":"h2","text":"Upsell and Promotion Powerhouse"},{"type":"p","text":"These displays are more than an order display. They can be leveraged to exponentially grow the sale of add-on items, featured combos, and limited-time offers. Visually appealing graphics and artwork with targeted messaging will guide your customers toward higher-margin items, helping to improve your bottom line without being too aggressive in the sale."},{"type":"h2","text":"Personalized customer experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Personalization is critical in this data age. Other advanced displays facing customers can be linked with loyalty programs. This can facilitate targeted promotions based on consumer preferences and buying habits. Just think about the visual: a waiting customer being displayed their favorite dessert that starts blinking right in front of them, a very subtle reminder that could trigger an additional sale."},{"type":"h2","text":"Build Brand Awareness and Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"These displays serve as a great medium through which to communicate and drive your brand identity. Bring them to the front by using a logo, brand colors, or even video bites of things telling the story about your restaurant. This kind of visual reinforcement strengthens brand recognition and creates a much more memorable customer experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Wrapping up the Potential: Tips about Effective Facing Guest Facing Displays"},{"type":"p","text":"Now, upon being convinced of the power of these displays, here are some tips to help ensure they deliver maximum impact:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Content is King (and Queen)"},{"type":"p","text":"The content you have in your CFD is paramount. Keep it clear, concise, and visually friendly. High-quality food shots, attention-grabbing fonts, and text that''s easy to read are must-haves. Keep refreshing it seasonally to keep things new and seasonal items highlighted."},{"type":"h2","text":"Location, Location, Location"},{"type":"p","text":"Place it right. Put your guest facing display highly in the line of vision but not to the point of obstructing the flow of traffic. So, think about the natural customer journey in your restaurant and place the displays accordingly."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep simple"},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid jam-packing these display systems with too many details. Only include what matters the most: sharp menus, facts regarding orders, and any announcement of relevance. Try avoiding the bombardment of customers with too many overwhelming animations and text."},{"type":"h2","text":"Embrace Technology, But Keep it User-Friendly"},{"type":"p","text":"But interactive features, like touchscreens, can take the customer experience to a whole new level. Just make sure that the interface is user-friendly and facile. Nobody wants to wrestle with an overcomplicated system when they are starving!"},{"type":"h2","text":"Metrics Matter"},{"type":"p","text":"Track and analyze the data brought in by your display facing the customers. See what type of content works best with your audience; based on this information, sculpt your message for the best effect."},{"type":"h2","text":"Close with a Bang: Take Your Restaurant to New Heights with Guest Facing Displays."},{"type":"p","text":"Use these tips and put the power of these displays to work for you. Interact with more exciting, efficient, and profitable dining experiences for your customers. Remember, happy customers mean repeat business and positive word-of-mouth marketing, the holy grail of any successful restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"So do not sell short the power of a well-used display. Put the investment in the best restaurant technology from eatOS, unleash your creativity, and make this next leap that takes your restaurant to customer satisfaction and success!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_b393ccae889945348757c445887229f5~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Insights', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-27', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('boosting-sales-and-profitability-with-point-of-sale-software-proven-strategies-aug-23', 'Supercharge Sales with the Best Point-of-Sale Software', 'Running a restaurant combines creative ideas in the kitchen, amazing service, and healthy profitability into one huge mix. Nowadays, though, even the most mouthwatering menu does not cut it in a competitive landscape....', '[{"type":"p","text":"Running a restaurant combines creative ideas in the kitchen, amazing service, and healthy profitability into one huge mix. Nowadays, though, even the most mouthwatering menu does not cut it in a competitive landscape. You need that secret weapon at your side, a powerhouse point-of-sale system."},{"type":"p","text":"Think of a point of sale like you would the central nervous system of your restaurant: it''s much more than just ringing up sales. With the right features and strategies in place, point-of-sale software can be the magic recipe for boosting sales, streamlining ops, and driving real profit to your bottom line."},{"type":"h2","text":"From Ringing Up Sales to Ringing in Profits"},{"type":"p","text":"Studies indicate that restaurants using Point of Sale software experience a revenue increase of up to 15%. This can be attributed to improved efficiency, faster service, and potentially higher order accuracy."},{"type":"p","text":"So how, exactly, does a restaurant point-of-sale save your business? Here''s how:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Shorter Waiting Time/Faster Sales"},{"type":"p","text":"Probably more than anything else, customers run out at the speed of Usain Bolt because of long lines and poor service. Point-of-sale helps take the roadblocks out of business, and this, in turn, simplifies the whole procedure of the transaction for personnel to be able to ring up sales both rapidly and effectively. Proper care of customers means that fewer will wait, yet satisfyingly many will orders fly away through the doors."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Have you ever run out of a key ingredient right at the peak dinner rush? No fun! The integration of such an inventory management capability within a point-of-sale system ensures that it keeps updating stock in real time. You''ll be able to automatically reorder points so that you never run out of one of your \\_ dishes. Plus, you''re going to get real insights as to what''s selling best, which will help optimize your stock."},{"type":"h2","text":"Data-Driven Decisions"},{"type":"p","text":"Data today in this very data-driven world, is power. It can easily be obtained through point-of-sale, pouring in data about customer history, popular menu items, and the times of the day when this restaurant happens to be laid. Being in this kind of goldmine will allow you to make critical business decisions: you will know where and how to upsell, and you will be in a position to design effective marketing campaigns and menu adjustments for maximal profit return."},{"type":"h2","text":"Loyalty Is a Two-Way Street"},{"type":"p","text":"You''ll be able to build customer loyalty, the most important factor behind a successful recipe for a restaurant. In-built loyalty programs within the point-of-sale software you use would help you to reward with points for the purchases made, give out discounts for all items ordered, and provide exclusive offers. Not only that, it keeps bringing back people as well as drawing new ones who share stories and keep calling others to come and have their special experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Leaning into the Value of Mobility"},{"type":"p","text":"Convenience is the thing that everyone is hunting for in today''s swift world. Mobile-friendly point-of-sale systems will let your staff take your orders right there, ridding you of the waiting time and thus providing a fabulous experience to the guests over a meal."},{"type":"h2","text":"Introducing the Hidden Gems: Advanced Point of Sale Features"},{"type":"p","text":"Except for the most elemental feature list, renting point-of-sale has a truly immense piling of advanced features to its credit. Here they are, in this respect:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Menu Management"},{"type":"p","text":"This makes it easy to experiment with new offerings, make seasonal changes, and even create, edit, and update the menu with pictures and descriptions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Employee Management"},{"type":"p","text":"It auto-tracks hours and performance, and cuts down the process of payroll to just a click button, all done within the system."},{"type":"h2","text":"Kitchen Display System"},{"type":"p","text":"The kitchen display system makes the communication process between the front of the house and the back of the house easier. The orders pop up digitally in the kitchen, thus avoiding errors, and making sure food goes out fast and right."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reporting and Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Dive deep into your sales data and turn customizable reports into insight about your most profitable menu items, peak sales hours, and customer demographics. That''s the information that will fire your data-driven decision-making to drive a more successful business."},{"type":"h2","text":"Pick the Right Point of Sale Software: Finding the Perfect Fit"},{"type":"p","text":"Today, it is like a nightmare to settle on the right one with point-of-sale providers springing up at every corner. Listed here are some highlights to put in focus:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Budget"},{"type":"p","text":"Point-of-sale is received at different price levels. Establish how much you are willing to spend and search for the best available option that corresponds to your demands within your budget."},{"type":"h2","text":"Your Restaurant''s Needs"},{"type":"p","text":"The size and type of your restaurant matter. What a small café using a short menu offers differs from what a big fine restaurant would like to have. Consider directly tailor-made software packages for your operation."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ease of Use"},{"type":"p","text":"A user-friendly interface is overall very important. Ensure that staff can easily navigate the software and run transactions smoothly."},{"type":"h2","text":"Scalability"},{"type":"p","text":"Think ahead. Move with the right kind of point-of-sale system through which your restaurant could grow."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"Hop into the future of restaurants with the right kind of point-of-sale from eatOS. No more waiting! Be sure to get the best point-of-sale software from us and bring to your restaurant the next level of success. A strong point-of-sale system paralleling it all is what fuels optimized operations and powers more sales, unlocking a world of insights based on data that helps restaurants rock and roll for years to come. After all, remember the saying from the competitive world of restaurants: an early bird who has smart technology gets the pound of flesh. Book a demo with us now."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_a0694e17cbcc4b0e81be202b381dcca8~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Growth', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-23', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-rise-of-online-ordering-how-technology-is-transforming-the-restaurant-industry-aug-22', 'The Delicious Revolution: Embracing the Future with Online Ordering', 'Do you remember flipping through phone books in hopes of finding a restaurant, then ordering by phone, only to hope and pray that the order came out just right? Yeah, those days are fading faster than a perfectly cooked...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Do you remember flipping through phone books in hopes of finding a restaurant, then ordering by phone, only to hope and pray that the order came out just right? Yeah, those days are fading faster than a perfectly cooked soufflé. We live in a world moving at breakneck speed, run by convenience, and right now, the whole restaurant industry is being deliciously disrupted by the rise of online ordering."},{"type":"p","text":"A spike in ordering online is not just some fad but a tenet change in customer behavior. Diners, and especially those from the millennial and Gen Z generations, always seek life''s conveniences and desire it in the fastest way possible. They surf through the menu, possibly customize orders, and pay for it all while sitting comfortably on their favorite couch (or in a park, or on a subway car - you catch my drift)."},{"type":"p","text":"This newfound control over the ordering process is a huge driver of why ordering online is taking off in such a big way. No more waiting on hold or battling restaurant background noise. With a few taps or clicks, a feast is on its way, freeing up precious time for customers to focus on other things, like scrolling through social media to decide what to eat next!"},{"type":"h2","text":"A Win-Win for Restaurants: Growth and Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"Ordering online proves beneficial not only for hungry customers alone; it acts as a game-changer for restaurants also. Studies indicate that restaurants implementing online ordering experience a significant sales increase, ranging from 10% to 30%. This growth can be attributed to increased order frequency, higher average order values, and attracting new customers who prefer online ordering convenience. The business advantages of using ordering online are as follows:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Increased Revenue"},{"type":"p","text":"Online ordering exposes your restaurant to a much larger market. Busy professionals, families balancing hectic schedules, and even those who just want to spend an evening in can now easily find out about your restaurant and order food from the comfort of their own home. This translates to more orders and by extension more money, your accountant will be pleased."},{"type":"h2","text":"Increases Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"Think of a world with no confusion from phone orders being lost or misunderstood in the mix. Online ordering systems reduce confusion in the ordering, freeing your staff to do what they do best, create culinary masterpieces."},{"type":"h2","text":"Data-Driven Decisions"},{"type":"p","text":"This one feature makes ordering online services packed with analytics, valuable. Keep track of customer preferences, know what a popular dish is, and when peak ordering periods are. That is a goldmine of data on which to base informed decisions about your menu, promotions, and staffing needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Marketing Magic"},{"type":"p","text":"Online ordering platforms often have built-in marketing tools in place that allow for everything from running targeted promotions and making special online-only offers to working in social media management to get the word out about your newest dishes."},{"type":"h2","text":"Adapting to the Future: Challenges and Considerations"},{"type":"p","text":"Naturally, no culinary revolution can be all roses and champagne. Here''s what you''ll have to keep in mind as you adapt your operation to ordering online in a shifting world:"},{"type":"p","text":"Most ordering online takes a commission on the order value. Include these as part of your pricing since the online channel still has to remain profitable."},{"type":"h2","text":"Delivery Logistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Working with a third-party delivery service, if you do not have a standing delivery of your own, makes the equation even more complicated. Couples need to stick with a trusted fleet that emphasizes the food quality and timeliness in which it is delivered."},{"type":"h2","text":"Optimizing the Menu"},{"type":"p","text":"An online menu needs to be easy to understand, unambiguous, and beautiful in its aesthetics. Good photographs do make all the difference to make customers make an order."},{"type":"h2","text":"Customer Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"A clean ordering experience should not end at ''place order.'' Ensure that the customer is aware of every step, especially the estimated delivery time, and provide a platform for ease of feedback."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Future is Flavorful: Embrace Online Ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"It''s not just a fad, online ordering is increasingly becoming the face of the future in the restaurant business. There is a great opportunity surrounding ordering online and its related technology that can not only streamline your operation but also ensure adherence and bring diners back for more."},{"type":"p","text":"Don''t stay in the digital dust! Begin the process of renovating your restaurant business in a convenience-friendly age by scheduling a demo with eatOS. Our ordering online platform financially fits your needs. With a little planning and the right tools from us, you''ll be able to turn your restaurant into an ordering online powerhouse, making sure great food is made accessible to a wider audience than ever before. So what are you waiting for? Begin your online ordering journey today with us and get ready to take your restaurant to a whole new level!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_c25af568161c4338b93d6ae62641a79a~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-22', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('cloud-based-kitchen-display-system-solutions-the-next-generation-of-kitchen-management-aug-21', 'Elevate Your Restaurant with Cloud-Based Kitchen Display Systems', 'Picture this: your restaurant, during the dinner rush. Online order platforms are popping up everywhere; the phones are ringing off the hook, and the front-of-house wait staff are all abuzz. In the eye of the storm,...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Picture this: your restaurant, during the dinner rush. Online order platforms are popping up everywhere; the phones are ringing off the hook, and the front-of-house wait staff are all abuzz. In the eye of the storm, your kitchen comes alive, and the din of sizzling pans, clattering utensils, and chefs moving in tune like the devil were watching. And somewhere in between all that activity, there is a sense of inefficiency: the huge stack of paper tickets, broken communication, and lost or delayed orders racking up minutes you don''t have to spare."},{"type":"p","text":"This happens way too often and is repeated in restaurants all over the place. Not anymore. The hero is here, and its cloud-based Kitchen Display Systems (KDS)."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ditch the Paper Trail, Embrace the Digital Age"},{"type":"p","text":"The cloud-based KDS solutions are ramping up kitchen management. Unlike the traditional paper ticket systems, this innovative one operates only online. KDS systems can help streamline communication between front-of-house staff and the kitchen. This leads to faster order preparation times by up to 20%. With orders from all sources, even the phone, streaming in real-time to the strategically placed digital displays in your kitchen, clutter and missed orders of the paper age are gone!"},{"type":"p","text":"How, indeed, does a cloud-based KDS simplify your life? Here''s a taste of the magic:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Real-time Update on Orders"},{"type":"p","text":"The orders will appear on the KDS right as they are placed, eliminating the need for you to write them yourself. The result is reduced errors, no more trying to figure out what some scribble says, and no waiting for that next batch of tickets to come out on the printer promptly."},{"type":"p","text":"The kitchen staff will be able to see the entire list of items that are on order and thus there will be no room for this kind of confusion. This could clear up incomplete and incomplete orders as far as their priority and completion time are concerned."},{"type":"h2","text":"Prioritization in Clicks"},{"type":"p","text":"Most of the cloud-based KDS will not only come with but also have inbuilt features about prioritization. You can command the system to give priority to the orders that have waited for some time, orders coming from large tables, or those from customers who have placed orders for hot items."},{"type":"h2","text":"Improved Fluidity of Work in the Kitchen"},{"type":"p","text":"By giving the chef a clear view of the order queue, this feature allows them to work optimally. Picture a line cooks who knows what will be needed at the critical stage: the ingredients will seamlessly change, and the chef will fill orders in less time."},{"type":"p","text":"There are cloud-based KDSs that sync with your inventory management system, allowing you to see what ingredients are running low and potentially receive alerts when items are out of stock, so at least a quick change to the menu can be enacted. No more unfortunate, mad, angry dashes to your grocer in the middle of lunch service!"},{"type":"h2","text":"Data-Driven Decisions for Success"},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to the above capabilities, cloud-based KDS touches supercharged, amazing data collection. With these systems tracking important metrics like how long it takes to complete an average order, item popularity, and menu item prep times, a restaurant truly never has to fly blind again."},{"type":"p","text":"This data can be quantitatively analyzed to understand where bottlenecks occur and get system behaviors adjusted accordingly. Information so derived can help in menu optimization, tell what dishes are most cost-beneficial, and even let you predict peak order times to ensure you have enough staff."},{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond Efficiency: A Boon for Customer Satisfaction"},{"type":"p","text":"The benefits associated with cloud-based KDS are long-reaching past kitchen doors. Faster order processing means faster service for your customers. This happy dance of streamlining and efficiency culminates in fast service, a delightful dining experience, and invariably, increased customer satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Scalability and Flexibility: Designed for Expansion"},{"type":"p","text":"Run a cloud-based system and you have none of those big upfront hardware costs. Just pay a monthly subscription fee, very affordable for restaurants of any size. Even better, these systems are brilliantly scalable. As your business grows, you can easily add new features or displays to accommodate the increased workload."},{"type":"h2","text":"Embrace the Future of Kitchen Management"},{"type":"p","text":"A simple fact: cloud-based KDS solutions are no longer just one more shiny gadget for kitchen management; they are revolutionary. Adopting an innovative solution like this will assist in making your kitchen a well-oiled machine: more efficient, more customer-satisfying, and on the fast track to success."},{"type":"p","text":"Ready to leave the paper chase in the past and walk into the future of kitchen management? Learn more about eatOS cloud-based KDS solutions today, and the ways that you could revolutionize your restaurant into a much more efficient one with us! Investing in our high-tech restaurant technology solution will help unlock a world of efficiency, data-driven insights, and ultimately a happier kitchen and thriving business end."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_3ed2fa1b9876407a8f5cfdd4034bc1bd~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-20', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('more-than-just-a-register-how-point-of-purchase-handhelds-can-boost-your-food-truck-order', 'Boost Your Food Truck Order with Point of Purchase Handhelds', 'Picture this: It''s a scorching summer day, and the aroma of your famous BBQ ribs wafts through the air, drawing in hungry customers. The line is forming fast, and you know that efficiency is key to keeping those bellies...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Picture this: It''s a scorching summer day, and the aroma of your famous BBQ ribs wafts through the air, drawing in hungry customers. The line is forming fast, and you know that efficiency is key to keeping those bellies happy and your profits soaring. Enter the handheld Point of Sale system, your secret weapon for navigating the chaos and maximizing your success."},{"type":"p","text":"From Order to Payment: A Seamless Symphony for Food Truck Order"},{"type":"p","text":"Gone are the days of scribbling orders on pads and fumbling with cash registers. Handheld Point of Purchase revolutionize the way you handle transactions, from the moment a customer steps up to your window to the final \"thank you\" and bite into their delicious meal. Here''s how these portable powerhouses enhance every step of your operation:"},{"type":"p","text":"Order Taking: Your staff can now roam freely, armed with handheld devices that effortlessly capture orders, even in the middle of a bustling crowd. This eliminates bottlenecks at the counter, ensuring faster service and happier customers. Special requests? No problem! They''re easily added to the order with a few taps, minimizing errors and ensuring customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"Payment Processing : Cash, credit, debit, mobile wallets - you name it, handheld Point of Sale systems can handle it all. This versatility not only expands your customer base but also eliminates the need to carry large amounts of cash, enhancing security. The lightning-fast transaction processing keeps the line moving, making those lunch breaks even more enjoyable for your customers."},{"type":"p","text":"Real-Time Inventory Tracking: Running out of ingredients is a food truck owner''s nightmare. According to a study, with handheld Point of Sale systems, food truck owners always know exactly what''s in stock, down to the last onion ring. This allows for better planning, timely restocking, and ultimately, less waste and happier customers who get to savor their favorite dishes."},{"type":"p","text":"Data-Driven Decisions: Handheld Point of Sale systems are not just transaction tools; they''re your personal data analysts. They track sales patterns, popular items, peak hours, and customer preferences, giving you valuable insights to make informed decisions about your menu, staffing, and marketing strategies. This data-driven approach can significantly boost your profitability and customer engagement."},{"type":"p","text":"Marketing on the Move: Ever wished you could reach out to those customers who raved about your gourmet grilled cheese? With handheld Point of Sale systems, you can. Some models integrate with email marketing tools, allowing you to capture customer information and send targeted promotions, loyalty rewards, or updates about your next location. This is a game-changer for building relationships and fostering loyalty."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the Transaction: Handheld Point of Sale systems do more than just process orders and payments. They enhance your brand image by showcasing a modern, tech-savvy approach. They streamline employee management, allowing you to track hours, sales performance, and even tips. They even make accounting a breeze with automatic reports and integrations with popular bookkeeping software."},{"type":"h2","text":"Investing in Your Future"},{"type":"p","text":"In the ever-evolving landscape of food trucks, staying ahead of the curve is essential. Embracing handheld Point of Sale systems is not merely an upgrade; it''s a strategic investment in your business''s future. By streamlining operations, enhancing customer experiences, and providing valuable data insights, these devices empower you to thrive in a competitive market."},{"type":"p","text":"So, are you ready to supercharge your food truck business? It''s time to ditch the outdated cash registers and embrace the future of mobile commerce. With a handheld Point of Purchase at your fingertips, you''ll be well-equipped to handle the lunch rush, delight your customers, and watch your profits sizzle. Connect with us today to schedule a product demo and a personalized consultation with our team."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_ea1e1f1b241c40e1a0ea5a06a8c9868a~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-19', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-management-systems-the-growth-engine-for-modern-dining-establishments-aug-5th', 'Restaurant Management System: The Growth Engine for Modern Dining', 'Imagine it: you, a charismatic restaurateur, this generation''s Willy Wonka, in your culinary world. Your brain fizzles with innovative dishes, your heart pounds for perfect service, and your restaurant is all a symphony...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Imagine it: you, a charismatic restaurateur, this generation''s Willy Wonka, in your culinary world. Your brain fizzles with innovative dishes, your heart pounds for perfect service, and your restaurant is all a symphony of delicious chaos. Something, however, is slicing your dream, the monstrous gremlin of disheveled inventory, endless waits for tables, and staff about to meltdown for good."},{"type":"p","text":"Then, out of nowhere, like a knight in shining armor, is the restaurant management system (RMS)."},{"type":"h2","text":"From Chaos to Calm: How Restaurant Management Systems Save the Day"},{"type":"p","text":"An RMS is way more than just a fancy-pants cash register. It''s front and center, digitally conducting the intricate dance of your restaurant''s operations, very much like the central nervous system, if you will, tacking at every turn key functions like POS."},{"type":"p","text":"This is your cash register on steroids. Whiz through orders, accept payments, , all the latest contactless options, and keep a sharp eye on your revenue."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Goodbye, jammed freezers and last-minute scrambles. RMS tracks your ingredients and inventory; it lets you know when supplies run low and even does smart ordering off sales trends. No more disappearing portions of that pricey truffle oil!"},{"type":"h2","text":"Table Management"},{"type":"p","text":"No more frustrated floating, looking guests around your front door. From reservations to tabletop flow and waitlist management, the RMS has you covered to ensure your customers leave happy and your tables keep turning."},{"type":"h2","text":"Staff Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Empower your staff! Employee scheduling, payroll, performance tracking, the RMS does it all. Even act as a training hub so that everyone understands your culinary vision."},{"type":"h2","text":"Customer Relationship Management (CRM)"},{"type":"p","text":"Recall that every Tuesday regular who likes to have extra pickles on their burger? The RMS remembers too. It captures customer preferences and purchase history, plus it takes care of the best-targeted loyalty programs, turning happy customers into raving fans."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reporting and Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Ever wondered which dish was a secret superstar or why sales dip on Tuesdays? RMS provides insightful reporting, turning your data into actionable knowledge to help you make data-driven decisions and optimize your menu, promotions, and even staffing levels."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Fun Factor: How Restaurant Management Systems Make Running a Restaurant Enjoyable"},{"type":"p","text":"An RMS is more than efficiency; it brings fun into the business of running a restaurant. Just imagine:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Freeing Up Your Time"},{"type":"p","text":"No more wrestling with spreadsheets or chasing down inventory lists. Remote monitoring automation gives you back that precious time, focusing on what matters: making amazing food experiences and a restaurant culture that rocks."},{"type":"h2","text":"Empower Your Staff"},{"type":"p","text":"Having a user-friendly RMS enables your team to focus on top-notch service. Let the system put in the hard work; let your staff shine with hospitality skills."},{"type":"h2","text":"Innovative Culture"},{"type":"p","text":"With the data and insights in your hands, you''re empowered to test new ideas on menus, pricing strategies that come with risks, and marketing campaigns. The RMS acts as a springboard for your creativity, keeping your restaurant ever-evolving, fresh, and exciting."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Final Course: Choosing the Right Restaurant Management System"},{"type":"p","text":"Well, the perfect RMS is only as good as that special ingredient that takes that signature dish of yours to a whole new level. Here''s how to choose the right system for your restaurant:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Your Restaurant''s Size and Needs"},{"type":"p","text":"A small cafe will not have the same needs as a large chain. Target an RMS that grows with your business, along with only the features required."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ease of Use"},{"type":"p","text":"Don''t get roped into the depths of some overly complicated system. The RMS should make sense, and be easy for you and your whole team to catch on and make use of right out of the box."},{"type":"h2","text":"Integration Capabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Does it integrate well with existing delivery services, accounting software, or online ordering platforms? Pretty seamless integration is what sets the tone for a smooth workflow."},{"type":"h2","text":"Budget"},{"type":"p","text":"RMS options range from free to very expensive. Figure out your budget and choose what gets you the most bang for the buck."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ready to Take Your Restaurant to the Next Level?"},{"type":"p","text":"Let not the gremlin of operational chaos prevail. Put a Restaurant Management System in the way of your establishment, and watch it develop. From beeline operation processes to empowered personnel and a data-driven take-off to success, an RMS will work as the growth engine your modern dining outlet is craving. So, kiss spreadsheets goodbye, embrace the digital revolution, and let your restaurant embark on a delicious journey to the top!"},{"type":"p","text":"Unleash your restaurant''s full potential with eatOS restaurant technology for managing your eatery with ease. Schedule a demo today with us and have the best RMS at your side, you''ll be able to transform your restaurant from a well-intentioned dream into a thriving culinary empire."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_4fe6bb0280304a47b28ed227f1aa74ca~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-15', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('quick-service-point-of-sale-systems-the-growth-engine-for-modern-fast-casual-restaurants-aug-4th', 'Fueling Growth: The Power of a Quick Service Point of Sale System', 'In a world of speed, fast casual, fast life, very hungry customers wanting super-fast service, applied, one needs the proper tools at their disposal. Here comes the Quick Service point of sale system: A technological...', '[{"type":"p","text":"In a world of speed, fast casual, fast life, very hungry customers wanting super-fast service, applied, one needs the proper tools at their disposal. Here comes the Quick Service point of sale system: A technological enigma that has become the beating heart of most modern restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"Imagine that: a busy rush at lunchtime, when the line winds down the counter like a capsular boa constrictor, and orders are yelled and meals prepped, all in one symphony. But instead of chaos, there''s a flatline. Orders are processed in seconds. Ingredients magically circumvent the lines to the cook line, and customers are off, merry, on their ways, with their tasty burritos or poke bowls, or whatever one might find in this culinary niche, less long than it takes to say \"hangry.\""},{"type":"p","text":"This, friends, is the power of a well-chosen quick-service point-of-sale system. Much more than just any cash register, it''s like an orchestra conductor, seamlessly coordinating every aspect of your operation, be it order taking, inventory management, or customer loyalty programs."},{"type":"p","text":"But how exactly is a quick service point of sale system able to become one? Let''s carve into the juicy details:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Speed Demons in the Kitchen"},{"type":"h2","text":"Lightning-Fast Order Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"Forget fumbling around with pen and paper. Point-of-sale systems for quick service provide intuitive order entry with customizable menus and modifiers. Consider this: tap a picture of a juicy burger and add cheese and bacon with one click - that''s the pace we''re talking about."},{"type":"h2","text":"Kitchen Display Systems (KDS)"},{"type":"p","text":"The kitchen display system relays the orders back to the kitchen, dispelling any possible miscommunication with each ingredient appearing magically at the right station. No chefs yelling to stand over and interpret unintelligible handwriting, just clear instructions and a clean workflow."},{"type":"h2","text":"Order Accuracy"},{"type":"p","text":"Say goodbye to frustrated customers who end up with pineapple on their pizza when they specifically asked for no pineapple all been there. Quick service point-of-sale systems reduce order errors, thus ensuring satisfaction and repeated visits."},{"type":"h2","text":"Happy Customers, Happy Business"},{"type":"h2","text":"Self-Order Kiosks"},{"type":"p","text":"Provide customers with an opportunity to be in charge of their experience. Using self-ordering kiosks, they will be able to view menus, customize orders, and pay without standing in a line. This minimizes waiting time but also brings convenience to the fans of technology, something that day by day involves more and more people."},{"type":"h2","text":"Loyalty Programs"},{"type":"p","text":"Provide better customer relationships. Point-of-sale systems are capable of integrating loyalty programs, which would mean rewarding repeat customers with points, discounts, and exclusive offers, like a pat on the back that keeps them coming for more."},{"type":"h2","text":"Mobile Ordering and Payment"},{"type":"p","text":"The future is now: order your food from your phone, skip the line. QSR point-of-sale systems that integrate with mobile ordering apps grant ultimate customer convenience, a big determinant factor in this fast-moving world."},{"type":"h2","text":"Management Magic"},{"type":"h2","text":"Real-Time Sales Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Gone are the days of waiting on those end-of-month reports. Point-of-sale systems for quick service restaurants now enable real-time sales data production that owners could use to track performance and trends and make educated decisions at a moment''s notice. Quite literally, just imagine in front of you the information of which menu items are flying off the shelves and which ones need some marketing love, all at your fingertips."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Never run out of your signature ingredients again. QSR point-of-sale systems allow inventory levels to be tracked, generate automatic reorder points, and even make educated predictions about future needs from your sales data. Less waste and tighter ops keep your customers happy, back with the \"second-best\" burrito, because you''re out of guac."},{"type":"h2","text":"Employee Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Empower your team and keep things running seamlessly. Many point-of-sale systems are equipped with hourly tracking as well as payroll management but also feature training modules. This lets you focus on what matters - building a tasty dining experience for your clients."},{"type":"h2","text":"Selecting the Appropriate System"},{"type":"p","text":"Because of its large quantity of choices, it could be paralyzing to choose the proper quick service point of sale system for your organization. Here are a few important things to help narrow down your choices:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Scalability: Does it have room to flex and grow with your business?"]},{"type":"ul","items":["Ease of Use: Will it be easy for your team to learn and put into action? Look for ease of use and intuitive interfaces."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Integration Capabilities: Has your tool got integration capabilities to be connected with other tools you run associated with customer loyalty management or accounting software?"]},{"type":"ul","items":["Cost: Look at both the upfront costs and ongoing maintenance."]},{"type":"h2","text":"Investing in Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"This advanced point-of-sale quick-service system is not just another point-of-sale hardware; rather, it is an investment in the long-term future of your fast-casual restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"Contact us at eatOS and book a demo with us. From allowing streamlining of operations to enhancing customer experience and even providing valuable data to help in making informed decisions, our point-of-sale system acts as that growth engine capable of propelling businesses toward success."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_2b2ebeb2804544fdbb810adca6c0eac8~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-14', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('maximizing-profitability-the-power-of-point-of-purchase-optimization-aug-3rd', 'Unleash Profits: Mastering Point of Purchase Optimization', 'Imagine this: a customer comes into your restaurant, and the smell of fajitas sizzling on a hot skillet hits them right away. Taking the menu, their eyes are scanning the descriptions that entice their taste buds,...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Imagine this: a customer comes into your restaurant, and the smell of fajitas sizzling on a hot skillet hits them right away. Taking the menu, their eyes are scanning the descriptions that entice their taste buds, exciting adjectives and mouthwatering food pictures. Hang on! Right before they even get to the main course, there''s this artfully placed churro display that catches their eye. Freshly fried, cinnamon sugar-dusted churros call from a nearby counter to make it pretty clear: gotta have churros for dessert!"},{"type":"p","text":"Well, this, my friends, is the magic of point-of-purchase optimization. It is the art, or, at least, the science, of guiding customer behavior at that magic moment they are about to make a purchase decision. According to a recent study by Brigham Young University study well-designed POP displays and signage increased sales by 20% for many businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Think about this: inside the checkout area of your favorite grocery store, you''ll find candy bars and other impulse buys lining up along the counter, beckoning you to throw them into your cart. That''s no accident. Retailers are pretty clear on the power of a properly placed POP display."},{"type":"p","text":"Now, let''s translate that power to your restaurant. Your POP system is not merely where the cash register happens to be, it''s at all the other places where your customer is exposed to more buying opportunities. Here''s how to unlock your restaurant''s POP landscape:"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. The Power of Suggestion"},{"type":"p","text":"People love suggestions, especially the edible kind. Here''s how you can implement suggestion selling at your POP:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Combo Meals: Bundle offers should be created, pairing profitable and high-margin items with your main courses. Reinforce this value proposition with prominent signage."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Upsell Through Attractive Displays: Display attractive desserts or appetizers near the main course ordering counter. Complement high-quality visuals with an appealing copy to prompt impulse buying."]},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. See It to Believe It"},{"type":"p","text":"The power of a visual sells itself. Here is how to capitalize on that visual appeal at the POP:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Attractive Display: Create visually appealing displays of your highest profit margin desserts, sides, or drinks. Just-baked and powdered sugar-dusted, brightly colored cocktails with tantalizing garnishes - create a visual temptation."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Digital Menu Boards: Use digital menu boards to create either mouthwatering videos or high-definition photographs of your dishes. Dynamic images move many more units than their static-menu counterparts."]},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Make it Easy, Make it a Habit"},{"type":"p","text":"Frictionless ordering and payment options encourage impulse purchases."},{"type":"ul","items":["QR Codes: Integrate QR codes in menus that allow them to order more items directly from their phones while they have a seat at the table."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Contactless Payment: Make sure a smooth checkout process is ensured with contactless payment options, like tap-to-pay. The faster and more painless it is to pay, the more likely they are to tack on that second dessert."]},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Don''t Forget the Power of the Staff"},{"type":"p","text":"Your staff is the biggest instrument you have in optimizing your POP. Here''s how you''ll empower them:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Product Knowledge: Educate your staff on the benefits and features of your highest-margin menu items. Empower them to make personalized recommendations and improve the customer experience."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Enthusiasm Is Contagious: They motivate positive attitudes and eagerness to suggest add-ons and specials. A kind smile and a warm \"Have you tried our signature cheesecake?\" work wonders all by themselves."]},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Measure and Adjust"},{"type":"p","text":"Data is your friend. Track sales trends and analyze exactly how specific techniques of POP impact your bottom line."},{"type":"ul","items":["A/B Testing: Test different POP strategies, whether it be display placement or signage, and see what speaks to your customers. Along the way, data-driven insights will help you tune in your approach."]},{"type":"h2","text":"The Final Bite"},{"type":"p","text":"Optimizing your point of purchase isn''t just about wringing extra bucks from your customers. It''s leading them through an exceptional dining experience that will leave them panting, and looking forward to more. After all, happy, well-fed customers mean loyal customers. So, tap into the force of POP and watch those profits, along with customer satisfaction, sizzle!"},{"type":"p","text":"Unlock your restaurant''s point-of-purchase secret sauce with eatOS. There''s no time like the present! Take a moment to update your existing POP program by scheduling a demo with us. Let your imagination and staff run wild, and harness the magic of suggestion selling. After all, a strategically placed churro never hurt!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_7d0258efdba442cb9f57478906c34f0c~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-12', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('scaling-your-restaurant-s-success-the-impact-of-kitchen-display-system-hardware-aug-1st', 'Revolutionize Your Kitchen with Advanced Display System Hardware', 'What keeps restaurants running in this dynamic field is efficiency and precision. Among the most important innovative tools involved in kitchen management is kitchen display system hardware. Specifically designed to...', '[{"type":"p","text":"What keeps restaurants running in this dynamic field is efficiency and precision. Among the most important innovative tools involved in kitchen management is kitchen display system hardware. Specifically designed to create accelerated operations, optimize all communications from the front of the house to the back, and much more, KDS hardware stretches out in the role of scaling success."},{"type":"h2","text":"Streamlining Operations with Advanced Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Gone are the days of handwritten tickets and manual order sorting. The integration of today''s KDS hardware with your restaurant''s point-of-sale system can seamlessly translate a digital order into a clear set of specific instructions that kitchen staff can follow. Not only do they reduce processing times for orders, but they almost eliminate errors, so each dish is cooked exactly to a customer''s specifications."},{"type":"p","text":"As per Restaurant Technology News, industry insights indicate that eateries with KDS hardware increase operational efficiency by up to 30% with a reduction in order fulfillment times. This additional efficiency not only improves customer satisfaction but also allows restaurants to service more covers during peak periods without their service standards being compromised."},{"type":"h2","text":"Improved Communication and Collaboration"},{"type":"p","text":"Effective communication is the backbone of any restaurant running smoothly. KDS hardware functions as one single hub where orders show in real-time to help kitchen staff gauge order urgency and dish complexity, allowing chefs, expediters, and servers to harmonize better with real-time transparency toward smoother workflow and even faster table turnover."},{"type":"p","text":"This research shows that restaurateurs using KDS hardware can report better communication between front-of-house and kitchen teams, reduce order errors, and raise the efficiency of the kitchen. These improvements don''t only smooth out operations; they enable staff to empower guests with memorable, cohesive dining experiences."},{"type":"h2","text":"Empowering Staff and Boosting Morale"},{"type":"p","text":"Besides operation efficiency, KDS hardware can help to empower the kitchen staff by giving them clear, organized instructions and greatly lessening the stress involved in trying to manage orders manually. Order routing will be automated with eatOS KDS hardware, setting out plainly what modifications to those orders have been requested, freeing chefs to strive toward culinary instead of administrative excellence."},{"type":"p","text":"Studies have shown that using KDS hardware improves staff morale, with staff reporting to show less stress and better satisfaction. This improves the culture at the workplace in general, hence a higher rate of staff retention and better productivity."},{"type":"h2","text":"Future-Proofing Your Restaurant with KDS Hardware"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant operations change with every update in technology. Advanced KDS hardware solves current operational challenges and dramatically future proofs your restaurant against upcoming trends. Predictive analytics, and further integration with AI tools, open pathways to smarter kitchens that not only know what their customers want but also how to allocate resources in the best way."},{"type":"p","text":"Industry experts estimate that advanced KDS hardware will be part of most operational strategies for full-service restaurants by 2025. Taking advantage of this technology shift not only keeps your restaurant atop innovation but also equips you with the tools necessary to aid in survival against competition."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion: Embrace Innovation and Ace Restaurant Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"This adoption of Kitchen Display System hardware hence does much more than give you a technological catch-up; rather, it is a strategic investment in the future success of your restaurant. From streamlined operations and better communication to staff empowerment and future-proofing in light of industry change, KDS hardware brings about tangible benefits right to the bottom line and customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"As you start the journey to expand your restaurant''s success, let us bear in mind the strength of KDS hardware acting as a game-changer in changing how things work within the kitchen by reducing lines and wait times, improving accuracy in orders, or boosting morale among staff, any of these aspects that a restaurant strives for. It is much better off with KDS hardware at the helm of operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Take the first step today into seeing just how KDS hardware can revolutionize your kitchen operations with eatOS. Your journey toward efficiency and customer satisfaction begins right here with us. Book a demo today!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_c53c642ae4964faea73de63044290a7e~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-09', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-technology-revolution-how-innovation-is-transforming-the-dining-experience', 'Revolutionizing Dining: The Impact of Restaurant Technology', 'The world of dining is being scaled anew, from cooking to dining, with the help of restaurant technology. Innovations implemented from kitchen to dining area revolutionize the way restaurants run and guests relate to...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The world of dining is being scaled anew, from cooking to dining, with the help of restaurant technology. Innovations implemented from kitchen to dining area revolutionize the way restaurants run and guests relate to their favorite eateries. These technological developments may greatly improve customer satisfaction and business growth for any restaurant owner or manager."},{"type":"p","text":"By 2032, the restaurant technology industry is projected to grow at a Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) of 14.24%, to a startling USD 37.62 billion. This notable expansion demonstrates how quickly technology is being adopted in the restaurant business."},{"type":"h2","text":"Welcome Restaurant Technology, The Game Changer"},{"type":"h2","text":"The Rise of Digital Ordering Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Among the various breakthroughs in the technology of restaurants, the digital ordering system is, perhaps, the one that offers the most innovation. This redefines the whole ordering process, with the customers ordering from kiosks, mobile applications, or online portals. This reduces the amount of time required to wait and errors in the order received, which eventually increases the satisfaction of their customers and leads to operational efficiency."},{"type":"h2","text":"Kitchen Display Systems: Improving Efficiency and Accuracy"},{"type":"p","text":"The other critical innovation in technology for restaurants is kitchen display systems(KDS). Replacing paper tickets, KDS is programmed to provide real-time updates of orders, facilitate communication between the front and back of the house, and ensure that orders are properly made and with the right timing deemed appropriate to minimize wait time and increase kitchen efficiencies."},{"type":"h2","text":"Point of Sale Systems: The Heart of Restaurant Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"The new point-of-sale systems are far from just being sophisticated cash registers. Modern point-of-sale systems are an all-encompassing package that has been appropriately integrated with many facets of restaurant management. It traces inventory, conducts sales analytics, and gives insights to aid restaurant owners in making the right decisions. In this way, point-of-sale systems automate operations for billing, reporting, or staff scheduling, letting the manager use time to develop customer experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Innovating Technologies to Improve Customer Experience"},{"type":"h2","text":"AI-Powered Chatbots: Making Customer Interactions More Personal"},{"type":"p","text":"AI''s power is finding an application in the food sector through AI-powered chatbots. They respond to queries, take orders, and even order in a very personalized way to deal with the customers. With such use of AI, restaurants can offer 24/7 support to make sure guests are catered for promptly, hence improving the dining experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Kiosks for Self-Service: Empowering Customers"},{"type":"p","text":"Self-service kiosks have also become very prominent across fast-casual and quick-service restaurants. Customers can scroll through menus and make orders on their own. Personalizing orders and completing payments is also possible. By putting customers in charge of their dining experience, self-service kiosks decrease wait time and free people to do other things like food preparation or better customer service."},{"type":"h2","text":"Mobile Apps: Convenience at Your Fingertips"},{"type":"p","text":"It is restaurant-specific mobile apps that make all the difference in customer interaction with their favorite dining places. Mobile applications provide features such as mobile ordering, loyalty programs, and tailored promotions. By using the power of convenience and ease, mobile apps drive customer engagement and loyalty, further increasing restaurants'' sales and revenues."},{"type":"h2","text":"Streamlining Operations with Leading-Edge Solutions"},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management Systems: Less Waste, Lower Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Proper inventory management is at the heart of any restaurant business. Modern inventory management systems utilize technology for restaurants to monitor stock levels and usage patterns and forecast future needs. This would optimize inventory levels to not have too much overstock, which ends in food wastage, yet not run out of stock on items required for customer service, which cuts down on costs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Employee Scheduling Software: Workforce Management at Its Best"},{"type":"p","text":"There is a lot of time spent in scheduling staff; it''s complex. Employee scheduling software automates shift assignments and tracks labor costs while easily allowing staff to cover shifts. Not only does it work toward better management of the workforce, but at the very same time, it would also ensure that a restaurant has the right kind of people working during peak hours. This directly means that customers are better handled and that the staff is also content."},{"type":"h2","text":"Contactless Payments: Safe, Convenient"},{"type":"p","text":"COVID-19 accelerated the growth of contactless payment options. Restaurants were forced to resort to contactless payment methods so their clientele could make safe and convenient transactions. In a nutshell, restaurants, through mobile wallets and tap-to-pay cards, reduce physical contact; hence, they avoid the transmission of germs in the interest of staff and customer safety."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Future of Restaurant Technology"},{"type":"h2","text":"Embracing Innovation for Long-Term Success"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant businesses are changing their phases at a fast pace. Staying on top of these technological innovations is the one that will keep restaurants buoyant in the long run. Not only will this technology for restaurants elevate the customer experience, but it will also streamline operations and bring about efficiency. With innovation sprouting at such a fast pace, restaurant owners and managers have to be at the forefront in purchasing these solutions to be at par in the market."},{"type":"h2","text":"Get a Head Start with the Latest Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Take your restaurant to the next level with cutting-edge technology for restaurants, be it digitized ordering systems, AI-based chatbots, more advanced inventory management, contactless payment methods, or anything else. Stay ahead of the wave with this landscape of innovation; shatter how you have traditionally viewed restaurant operations and take a good dining experience into your customers'' lives."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion: Fast-track Your Restaurant Today"},{"type":"p","text":"Innovation of this technology for restaurants significantly transforms the dining experience; it becomes the foundation of opportunity for customer satisfaction and operational efficiency enhancement. It simply means that being a restaurant owner or manager, it''s important to keep keeping up with technology coupled with leveraging it. Without waiting much, just initiate searching the current restaurant technology solutions, and you will observe the outstanding business turnaround."},{"type":"p","text":"See how the latest technology paves the way to transform your restaurant. Contact us at eatOS today to find out how innovative solutions can transform operations and delight customers."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_0fef9d4dfe724c38bd1989b33aec78f1~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-07', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('maximizing-efficiency-and-profitability-the-power-of-an-all-in-one-point-of-sale-system-aug-29', 'Boost Efficiency and Profits with an All-In-One Point of Sale System', 'Operating a restaurant is like a whirlwind. From managing the staff to taking orders and keeping everything working smoothly, it feels like you are running around in circles. What if there was a way to fine-tune your...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Operating a restaurant is like a whirlwind. From managing the staff to taking orders and keeping everything working smoothly, it feels like you are running around in circles. What if there was a way to fine-tune your whole operation, boost efficiency, and watch profits go off the roof? Introducing the all-in-one point of sale: your modern hero of restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"The global point-of-sale system market is projected to reach a staggering USD 42.5 billion by 2027, reflecting a Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) of 9.02%. This significant growth indicates the increasing demand for these integrated solutions. Ditch that clunky, archaic cash register and mountains of spreadsheets. A true all-in-one point-of-sale system acts like a conductor, bringing every function of your restaurant into perfect harmony."},{"type":"h2","text":"Challenge Accepted: Common Pain Points Restaurants Face"},{"type":"p","text":"Every restaurateur knows the pain points-what inefficiencies rob from profits and make owners feel overwhelmed. Here are just a few culprits:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Slow Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Manual order-taking and processing create long lines and frustrated customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management Headaches"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a constant fight to keep track of the stock, eliminate waste, and know when to replace your materials with fresh stock."},{"type":"h2","text":"Limited Sales Data"},{"type":"p","text":"When there isn''t enough data to back up your ideas, it''s difficult to make informed decisions about your menu and marketing strategies."},{"type":"h2","text":"Disjointed Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"Systems for inventory, sales, and staff management only result in more chaos and communication breakdowns."},{"type":"p","text":"These can make running a restaurant feel like an uphill battle."},{"type":"h2","text":"All-In-One Point of Sale: Your Restaurant''s Efficiency Engine"},{"type":"p","text":"An all-in-one point-of-sale system is a bit like a magic box for your restaurant. Automating key processes keeps your restaurant humming along even smoother, and in several ways, it revs up your bottom line. This is done by offering:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Faster Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Now customers can electronically place their orders to reduce wait times and increase table turns."},{"type":"h2","text":"Inventory Management Made Easy"},{"type":"p","text":"Real-time tracking helps you reduce stockouts and food waste to save you money."},{"type":"p","text":"Data-driven insight at the tips of your fingers"},{"type":"p","text":"Comprehensive sales reports give you an eye on customer behaviors and sales trends to enable data-driven decisions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Unified Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"Control everything from your inventory and staff scheduling to customer loyalty programs, right within one central system."},{"type":"h2","text":"Increased Staff Productivity"},{"type":"p","text":"Free up staff hours from manual tasks to focus on delivering exceptional customer experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"This all-in-one point-of-sale system lets you forget the headaches of operationality and get back to running a slick, efficient restaurant that keeps your customers happy and your profits ticking over."},{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond Efficiency: The Unexpected Advantages of a Point of Sale System"},{"type":"p","text":"While streamlined operations and happy customers are major wins, an all-in-one point-of-sale system delivers more than this. Here are some extra unexpected benefits for your consideration:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Better Customer Experiences"},{"type":"p","text":"Mobile ordering, loyalty programs, and digital receipts all help drive ease and delight into the customer experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Happier Staff"},{"type":"p","text":"Easy-to-use technology empowers your staff and can increase job satisfaction while decreasing stress."},{"type":"h2","text":"Less Paperwork"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital receipts and inventory tracking reduce clutter and save space, trees, and your sanity."},{"type":"h2","text":"Scale for Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"All-in-one Point-of-Sale solutions will scale your restaurant business as it continues to grow, adding features and functionality as you see necessary."},{"type":"h2","text":"Is an All-in-One point-of-sale Solution the Right Solution for Your Restaurant?"},{"type":"p","text":"Even while all-in-one point-of-sale systems offer many benefits, you still need to take your specific demands into account. The following are some inquiries you should pose to yourself:"},{"type":"p","text":"What kind and what size of restaurant are you running? Available point-of-sale systems range from basic solutions for small cafes to large restaurants having feature-rich systems."},{"type":"p","text":"How much can you afford to spend? While point-of-sale systems have different price tags, be assured that there will be one within your pocket."},{"type":"p","text":"What features do you want to have in a system? Think of your needs specifically and seek a system that gives you those features."},{"type":"h2","text":"Drive Efficiency: Getting Started with an All-in-One point of sale System"},{"type":"p","text":"Now that you are powered up for a point of sale, research some different options and choose the one that best suits your needs and your pocket. Here are some other tips:"},{"type":"p","text":"Read Real Customer Reviews: See what other restaurateurs are saying about various point-of-sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Schedule Demos: Get firsthand experience, most point-of-sale companies will let you try their system for free before you buy."},{"type":"p","text":"Ease of Use: Ensure that you find a system with an interface where your employees will be able to learn easily."},{"type":"p","text":"Ensure it Scales: Look for a point-of-sale system that grows variably with your business as requirements change."},{"type":"p","text":"Delay No Longer; Get in Control with an All-in-One Point of Sale System from eatOS Now!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_ce7c971e43534f2ca966157b7c4e3036~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Growth', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-06', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('why-upgrading-your-pos-technology-is-essential-for-restaurants', 'The Benefits of Upgrading Your POS Technology', 'Customer expectations shift and technology advances, the restaurant industry must embrace that new technology to stay in competition. Trends indicate that consumers increasingly favor personalization, quickness and...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Customer expectations shift and technology advances, the restaurant industry must embrace that new technology to stay in competition. Trends indicate that consumers increasingly favor personalization, quickness and accuracy: Diners prefer automation, fast yet exceptional service, trendiness, healthy options, and explicitly allergy- and diet-friendly menus."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants need to consider these factors when they are Ready to move on from their current POS system? Some of the key features that your new POS should include are:"},{"type":"p","text":"\\- Allergy information at guest’s fingertips"},{"type":"p","text":"\\- Quick order taking through a handheld device"},{"type":"p","text":"\\- Digital receipts"},{"type":"p","text":"\\- Kiosk or tablet ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"\\- Multilingual support"},{"type":"p","text":"Implementing a new POS system can be a big investment for a restaurant. Not only do you have to purchase the hardware and software, but you also need to train your staff on how to use it. However, if you want to stay competitive in the ever-changing restaurant industry, upgrading your POS system is essential. With the right POS system in place, you can improve your guest’s experience, increase efficiency, and make better business decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"If you are looking for a new POS system for your restaurant, be sure to check out eatOS Restaurant POS. eatOS offers all of the features mentioned above and more, making it the perfect POS system for any restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant technology is constantly changing and evolving, so it''s important to stay up-to-date on the latest trends. Upgrading your POS system is a great way to do that. With the right POS system in place, you can improve your guest experience, increase efficiency, and make better business decisions. So what are you waiting for? Upgrade your POS system today!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_690a96705492474686ed0e2100d241fe~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-02', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('point-of-sale-the-savior-of-small-business', 'Point of Sale: The Savior of Small Business', 'Advanced Point of Sale systems have revolutionized small restaurants by streamlining operations, saving costs, and giving them the opportunity to grow and scale. Shop around for the POS that fits your restaurant’s...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Advanced Point of Sale systems have revolutionized small restaurants by streamlining operations, saving costs, and giving them the opportunity to grow and scale. Shop around for the POS that fits your restaurant’s specific needs, and it will prove an invaluable business tool even as the marketplace evolves."},{"type":"p","text":"QuickOrder on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Get More with a Smart Point of Sale"},{"type":"p","text":"While POS terminals used to serve as little more than registers, now they come with so much more. Get a barcode scanner, smart card reader, printers for both the front and back of house. and so much more depending on what your business needs and your budget allows."},{"type":"p","text":"Track your inventory and sales with eatOS technology, which automatically generates relevant sales reports. Identify patterns in traffic and ordering trends so you can strategically price food and deliver quality customer service. Push best-selling dishes or create promotions around menu items that don’t do so well. Do profits tend to dip on Wednesday evenings? Then host an unlimited pasta special based on your customers’ favorite linguini dish to give revenue a boost."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also instantly update your menus to tweak prices or remove sold-out options, thus providing accurate information for the best quality of service."},{"type":"h2","text":"Payment Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"Efficient transactions require eatOS agnostic payment processors, which work faster than your traditional card readers and let you take any kind of payment the customer wants. From mobile wallets to credit cards to tap or swipe to pay, eatOS speeds up the process so customer experiences end on a high note. Never turn down a guest just because you can’t take their preferred payment method."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS automates accounting too. Don’t have to spend so much time doing it manually and run up exorbitant, unnecessary labor costs. We automatically run payroll, and even consider different pay rates and overtime as well as their tips, so your accounting is fast and efficient every quarter."},{"type":"h2","text":"Scheduling and Workforce Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Creating weekly or biweekly schedules is yet another time-consuming manual task that eats away at your management team’s productivity. With eatOS Point of Sale, you get software integrations with 7Shifts, which not only automates and streamlines scheduling efficiency but makes it easy for your workers to trade shifts online."},{"type":"p","text":"Monitoring sales data lets you see which employees sell the most on average so you can create better marketing strategies and identify who deserves a raise."},{"type":"h2","text":"Diversify Services with a Point of Sale"},{"type":"p","text":"With a smarter system, you can expand your website to offer various new sales opportunities that cater to the marketplace as it’s changed since the pandemic. People now rely more frequently on online options, so why not offer more on your website?"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Collect all the data from delivery, takeout, and curbside services on one comprehensive POS report."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Sell gift cards that guests will redeem when dine-in services resume, thereby keeping them engaged in the meantime."},{"type":"p","text":"3. Offer virtual experiences to make up some profit lost when dine-in services closed, like cooking classes or meal kit subscriptions."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Small businesses that rely on smart Point of Sale systems can grow and scale freely. With its associated devices, capabilities, and software integrations, restaurants work more efficiently when their POS technology is up to speed."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS offers an all-in-one cloud-based eco-system exclusively for restaurants. From Point of Sale to Contactless Ordering, Pay & Order at Table, Kitchen Display System, Guest Facing Display, Online Ordering APP / Website and Workforce Management there is everything to help a restaurant succeed no matter the size. Click Here to Schedule a demo to learn more about how your restaurant can make a smooth transition into the world of restaurant technology made simple."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #Restaurant #RestaurantBusiness"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_1071183041b24c7c92cb9d676d4f269a~mv2.jpeg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-06-01', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-right-pos-hardware-for-full-service-restaurants', 'The Right POS Hardware for Full Service Restaurants', 'When it comes to managing your full service restaurant, you need the best of the best technology on the market to effectively handle any obstacle that comes your way. In the food service industry especially, unexpected...', '[{"type":"p","text":"When it comes to managing your full service restaurant, you need the best of the best technology on the market to effectively handle any obstacle that comes your way. In the food service industry especially, unexpected challenges crop up all the time. Having the tools you need to properly overcome any trouble that occurs is vital to smooth operations, and that starts with the right Point of Sale system that supports your customers as well as business."},{"type":"p","text":"Both day-to-day and in the long term, eatOS is here to help bring every full service restaurant up to speed and into the future."},{"type":"h2","text":"Clear Data Means Better Business Decisions"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced Point of Sale systems like the one powered by eatOS helps everyone in the chain of command, from owners down to every individual server. We track sales data and give real-time, analytic reporting that make it easy to make better decisions. Our heat mapping capabilities identify and highlight trends throughout the day so you can better forecast sales and make applicable business decisions, such as when to schedule more or less staff than usual, menu changes to optimize sales, and more."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reduce Labor Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Full service restaurants can better manage how much they spend on staffing and labor costs when theyre equipped with the most cutting-edge devices available. Save money instantly just by automating certain aspects of the business. For example, scheduling traditionally takes up a significant amount of effort which in turn costs the business money. Free up managers’ time by investing in eatOS technology, which we’ve integrated with 7Shifts to make it easy for workers to trade shifts with each other, submit time off requests and more, all without bothering management for approvals. Operations run smoother with advanced software and hardware working together with your Point of Sale."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reduce Food Waste"},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS offers inventory management capabilities as well. Track your stock with real-time reporting that lets you know when and what to order so you never have to turn customers away because you’re out of the necessary ingredients that make up their favorite dish. Enhanced communication between the front and back of house also reduces food waste. Knowing what you have in abundance lets you know to order less of it in the future or begin promotional campaigns designed to push sales up for dishes that contain that ingredient. Either way, optimize your money management with inventory tracking."},{"type":"p","text":"When you combine mobile Point of Sales with Kitchen Display Systems, communication within your team reaches all-new heights. Don’t waste money and hurt the environment with excess food waste; let technology bridge the gap."},{"type":"h2","text":"Upselling Capabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Maximize the potential sales on every customer that comes in. While you can train servers to offer sides and modifications, even the most seasoned worker can forget when theyre in a rush. Our devices automatically prompt upselling to increase the average check size, get servers better tips and improve the guest experience with increased personalization. Customizing every order makes guests feel more understood and valued, thus improving individual customer relationships and encouraging repeat visits."},{"type":"p","text":"Make every order more accurate and get dishes out to their tables faster. Decrease how often food gets sent back or comped while simultaneously encouraging guest loyalty. Even the checkout process runs smoother when you can split bills and items with the press of a button, as tableside ordering and transaction capabilities mean that customers dont have to wait for the check which then improves table turn times too."},{"type":"h2","text":"Better Guest Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Manage the flow of your customers by strengthening your hold over your service areas. Create a detailed floor plan to help hosts and servers seat customers, give a more accurate estimate about wait times, and handle reservations with ease. Guest management is an extremely important aspect of customer service which is why it’s so vital to meet their needs and expectations, and ensure every experience they have with your restaurant is a good one. With so much competition out there, fostering loyalty should be one of your biggest concerns as a restaurateur."},{"type":"p","text":"That’s why eatOS grows your online ordering channels to encourage more takeout and delivery. Sync these directly with your dine-in sales on the PoS so you always have an accurate, real-time idea of how your business is doing."},{"type":"p","text":"Our cloud-based technology lets you access your restaurant’s data from anywhere as long as there’s an internet connection. This keeps your data secure but accessible so you can run your business without worry. Adjust pricing based on sales data, update the daily special, run promotional campaigns and check on the health of your business on-the-go. We know you’ve got a busy schedule, and eatOS is here to make restaurant management easy. When it comes to managing your full service restaurant, only the best of the best technology will do."},{"type":"p","text":"There’s only one food service technology company that can handle your full service restaurant’s needs. Contact eatOS today and book a demo to find out what else we can do to bring your restaurant into the future."},{"type":"p","text":"#RestaurantTechnologyandCOVID19 #eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #CloudTechnology #Restaurants"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_f95f5f6f8ba04ba787dc05f667176ff7~mv2.jpeg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-30', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('community-highlight-my-green-lunch', 'Community Highlight: My Green Lunch', 'When Todd Evjenth started My Green Lunch in 2012, he aimed to feed delicious, organic food to local schoolchildren in Silicon Valley. However, once the COVID-19 pandemic touched down in the area and necessitated...', '[{"type":"p","text":"When Todd Evjenth started My Green Lunch in 2012, he aimed to feed delicious, organic food to local schoolchildren in Silicon Valley. However, once the COVID-19 pandemic touched down in the area and necessitated shelter-in-place protocols, there were suddenly no schools in the area to helpbut still plenty of children in need. For that reason, the lunch catering company decided to turn its attention to the community at large."},{"type":"p","text":"In a statement, Evjenth confirmed, “My Green Lunch has completely shifted our focus from providing healthy school lunches to providing healthy emergency meal relief. They’ve partnered with the Office of Education in Santa Clara County as well as Loaves & Fishes Family Kitchen, a soup kitchen in San Jose, to take on the added responsibility of a wider scope. As of 9 April 2020, they’ve fundraised $30K out of their total goal of $300K and provided 5,450 meals to Northern California. Their hope, moving forward, is to perfect the partnership to the point where they can provide 2,500 free meals every week to the Bay Area community."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where do they deliver?"},{"type":"p","text":"When the local schools shut down and My Green Lunch developed their new community outreach plan, they worked hard to adapt quickly so they could return to helping those in need. They repurposed some of their old equipment for new use; their van, for instance, quickly become a staple of the initiative as one of the main ways they bring food to different communities. To supplement what My Green Lunch already had, Loaves & Fishes Family Kitchen similarly repurposed their À La Carte van to cover their portion of the delivery route."},{"type":"p","text":"My Green Lunch and its partners developed a schedule to help both themselves and the communities that they serve. A consistent plan about where they will be on which day allows the partners organize their resources and lets the households that they serve plan out their food intake and storage for the week between deliveries."},{"type":"p","text":"They distribute the food at a different school each day of the week. The Santa Clara County Office of Education also gives out food every Thursday and Friday."},{"type":"h2","text":"What do they serve?"},{"type":"p","text":"My Green Lunch began their initiative as a means of getting healthier food into schools. Their website describes the company as “proud members” of the Community Alliance for Family Farmers, further demonstrating their dedication to helping the public. The page also touts their dedication to “meet the dietary needs and restrictions of all students, including gluten free, nut free (of course!), dairy free, vegetarian, and vegan options in our menu offering.”"},{"type":"p","text":"They have not forgotten their healthy purpose despite shifting from school-aged demographics to the larger community in need. Instead, they’re as fiercely committed to being environmentally friendly as ever and seek to bring that greenness to everyone they now serve. With compost-friendly packaging, napkins and utensils, they maintain a more sustainable carbon footprint and benefit not just the community but the earth as well."},{"type":"h2","text":"How can you help?"},{"type":"p","text":"Although the partnerships with Loaves & Fishes and the Santa Clara County Office of Education give My Green Lunch the resources necessary to reach more people, they still can’t carry out their mission without additional aid. That’s why they’ve set up a GoFundMe campaign so that individuals who can afford it can donate toward the greater good of those less fortunate in their area."},{"type":"p","text":"My Green Lunch’s campaign page states that all donations help them pay “for sourcing ingredients, meal preparation and meal delivery to dedicated drop-off locations” to give contributors a clear idea of where their money goes. These meals are all prepared in a designated kitchen in San Jose, allowing the company to continue sourcing ingredients from local, organic family farms which allows them to not only serve the community and the planet, but these hardworking businesses as well."},{"type":"p","text":"As the donation page states their story, they also make their goals clear: “For every $5 donated, you will be providing 1 meal to someone in need. Our goal of $300,000 will enable My Green Lunch to provide up to 60,000 meals over the course of the COVID-19 pandemic. We can produce 3,000-5,000 meals a day, so with the $300,000 this ensures our ability to provide our target number of meals.”"},{"type":"p","text":"As this pandemic continues and My Green Lunch strives toward their goal of providing 60K meals to Northern California, people with the means and drive to help can show their support by donating to My Green Lunch’s GoFundMe page."},{"type":"p","text":"With schools shut down and many families wondering how best to support and feed their kids, initiatives like the one created by My Green Lunch and its partner organizations double down in their commitment to better the environment, contribute to organic family farms and assist the local communities where they have always dedicated their time. Everyone should strive to prioritize compassion and outreach as we struggle through COVID-19 together, and we can look toward initiatives like the one created by My Green Lunch for good examples of how to proceed."},{"type":"p","text":"#CommunityOutreachStrategies #CoronavirusPandemic #Covid19Pandemic #Delivery #FoodService"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_e781a99367ab46608ded6a0b6da7ce84~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-26', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('consider-partnering-with-these-third-party-apps', 'Consider Partnering With These Third Party Apps', 'Skip to Main Content', '[{"type":"p","text":"Skip to Main Content"},{"type":"p","text":"Delivery has risen in popularity as the COVID-19 pandemic continues. With shelter-in-place measures forcing everyone indoors, making people scared to go to the grocery store and forbidding dine-in services at restaurants across the world, many have increased how often they order in. Most restaurants previously placed their focus on dine-in services and didn’t pay as much attention to delivery. Now, though, that’s the only revenue stream they have coming in."},{"type":"p","text":"Whether you’re new to online ordering services or just shifting focus for the first time, a third party app can massively help your business. Because these apps already have an audience and make it easy to find your restaurant, you don’t have to spend money and time promoting your name. The brand recognition comes with the territory. On top of cutting startup costs and providing you with a built-in customer base, certain third party platforms have particular appeal to restaurants because of partnership benefits Many currently offer additional perks to help restaurants contend with the growing concerns over COVID-19."},{"type":"p","text":"Here are some third party delivery platforms helping out the community, restaurants and customers alike:"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Postmates"},{"type":"p","text":"Postmates published an alert reminding everyone to wash their hands and protect themselves from the potential spread of disease. Aside from this notice, like many platforms they decided to implement a non-contact delivery option. Rather than knocking and handing over an order like usual, workers can now drop off food at the door and let the customer know via text or call that their order has arrived. By giving them the option to eliminate face-to-face contact, delivery workers and customers both avoid the potential spread of infection and abide by the six foot social distancing guideline without compromising service."},{"type":"p","text":"In case someone does fall ill, the app has also created the Postmates Fleet Relief Fund to give workers access to preventative care, testing, medical expenses and check-ups. This ensures the continued wellness and safety of delivery drivers. Drivers can also receive extra assistance from the Fund if they get sick, which covers two weeks’ worth of lost income. To protect their customers, Postmates will also put workers’ accounts on hold if they test positive for COVID-19, a suspension that lasts until the incubation period ends and they make a full, confirmed recovery."},{"type":"p","text":"Postmates has further implemented a Small Business Relief Pilot, currently tested in the San Francisco Bay Area. Small businesses there have waived commission fees so they can deliver to customers at no cost to the business. Postmates is currently looking to expand this program to other areas, too."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Grubhub"},{"type":"p","text":"Grubhub has deferred commission fees for independent restaurants affected by this crisis. CEO Matt Mahoney said, “Delaying our revenue will increase the restaurant’s cash flow, allowing them to pay their employees and weather this difficult situation.” Grubhub has set aside up to $100 million for this endeavor, and restaurants will have as long as four weeks to repay the fees after the suspension gets lifted."},{"type":"p","text":"They also implemented a Smart Promotions feature. For every dollar that restaurants invest in growth, Grubhub will match it. This aims to double the effectiveness of promotion to help restaurants garner business at a time when they need it most."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. uber eats"},{"type":"p","text":"Uber Eats waived delivery fees for all of their customers, which encourages them to order from merchants on the app. They further provide free meals to first responders and healthcare workers, demonstrating their appreciation for their work in this extremely difficult time and giving back to them as they help everyone in the community."},{"type":"p","text":"The platform also provides assistance to their workers during this crisis. They’ve also implemented a “leave at the door” delivery option. To further prevent the spread of COVID-19 and other diseases, Uber is giving disinfectant to their workers; as they struggle to meet the demand for sanitation, the company will prioritize those in major cities first in the hopes of curbing the disease in the worst-affected and highest-populated areas."},{"type":"p","text":"When workers do get sick or exposed, Uber Eats suspends the driver’s account and provides them with two weeks of financial assistance to avoid people coming to work sick due to financial concerns and a lack of options."},{"type":"p","text":"They published a safety guide on their website that breaks down how drivers, delivery workers, customers and restaurants can each stay healthy. Along with this, the webpage also provides additional resources so people can support drivers and restaurants during this time."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. door dash"},{"type":"p","text":"DoorDash put a twist on contactless delivery by implementing it, not only as an option, but as the default. Customers have to deliberately opt in to face-to-face delivery now, and even still drivers can change over to contactless at any time by simply confirming it with the customer via call or text. This puts power into the workers’ hands and lets them control their own health and safety. Although this, like many of the measures that third party apps have started using, was invented to combat the spread of COVID-19, this feature has the potential to last long after mandatory self-isolation measures lift. People will likely show a lot more caution toward contact and the spread of all diseases in the future."},{"type":"p","text":"If a worker does contract COVID-19 or have to quarantine by law, DoorDash will provide them two weeks’ pay to make up for the lost wages. They also give supplies to workers in areas affected by the disease, such as hand sanitizer, gloves and wipesall highly coveted items in short supply at the grocery store."},{"type":"p","text":"Furthermore, DoorDash aims to assist affected restaurants by earning them a projected $200 million in additional sales this year. For merchants new to the app, DoorDash now offers a 30-day reprieve from commission fees when they sign up. Unlike Grubhub, this is not a deferral but a complete waiver; they never have to pay back those fees. This will greatly help restaurants improve sales and attract customers without worrying about owing a future debt. DoorDash also works with restaurants to help them improve their food prep protocols to ensure that their workers, merchants and customers all stay as safe as possible."},{"type":"p","text":"They have additional benefits for restaurants already on the app. Current partners pay no commission on pick-up orders anymore, and certain eligible merchants will notice a lower commission fee on delivery as well. DoorDash also announced that they aim to add “more than 100,000 independent restaurant partners to DashPass  our subscription program which offers $0 delivery for consumers  for free.” This is huge for restaurants, as DashPass provenly generates a lot more sales than the regular app."},{"type":"p","text":"DoorDash also owns Caviar, another delivery service; by lowering commissions for DashPass merchants and attracting more customers to the platform, Caviar could afford to waive its delivery fee for everyone as well."},{"type":"p","text":"DoorDash further set aside $20 million for merchant marketing to help generate more sales. They’re doing everything they can to support their drivers and help local restaurants stay open, too."},{"type":"p","text":"With quarantines still going strong and people growing more scared to leave the house, delivery apps are a great way to keep your restaurant running despite the closure of dine-in services. These four platforms, along with many others, sacrifice profit in this time of widespread need to help the community and merchant partners that keep them in business."},{"type":"p","text":"Many service providers like eatOS integrate with third party apps like these to keep your restaurant running efficiently. Subscribe with us to learn more about keeping the community safe and healthy."},{"type":"p","text":"#CoronavirusPandemic #OnlineOrdering #FoodService #ThirdPartyApps #Restaurants"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_7403e60787fd4aa4901c712425d7cb68~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-24', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('invest-in-developing-your-staff', 'Invest in Developing Your Staff', 'Your staff is the most integral part of your business: They’re the face, hands and lifeblood of the company. This is true of any small business, but low-level employees are especially crucial to the food service...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Your staff is the most integral part of your business: They’re the face, hands and lifeblood of the company. This is true of any small business, but low-level employees are especially crucial to the food service industry which relies on customer service and quality attitudes to really make a customers experience greatthough of course, you need good food, too."},{"type":"p","text":"Considering the high turnover rate in the restaurant industry, which averages around 75% across the board and nearly 150% for QSRs alone according to the 2019 Bureau of Labor Statistics, it makes sense that building an efficient team is even more critical for restaurants than it is for other small businesses. Investing in the professional development of your workers is in your best interest because employees, especially those in the younger generations, overwhelmingly prefer jobs that in some way benefit their professional development. They’re interested in gaining skills that will foster an upwards trajectory throughout their career."},{"type":"p","text":"This drive is valuable to you as well and is a fantastic jumping off point to begin mentoring them in their personal and professional development. Youll end up with better workers who can in turn teach new hires the ropes; investing in this kind of cyclical improvement is especially good, if you can achieve it, because it helps you hang on to employees for longer. In an industry plagued by turnover, that’s difficult to achieve and precious to have."},{"type":"p","text":"How exactly can management invest in developing their staff?"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Set goals"},{"type":"p","text":"Employees can’t improve if they don’t know the standard to which they’re meant to aspire. When they have a tangible goal, they focus on that and become more productive as a result. Thus having relevant, achievable endgames are hugely beneficial to a restaurant. If you can identify the areas that need the most improvement within your establishment, you can begin to set applicable goals to remedy those situations."},{"type":"p","text":"Your objectives can have any time frame, although typically smaller is better. For this reason, quarterly reviews are more beneficial than annual reviews because it’s easier to track progress and see whether these goals are being met, and reassess, reassign goals if necessary, or try alternative strategies for meeting them if the current system doesnt work. Monitoring progress is a careful balance of giving staff time and space to improve but still checking in often enough to track and give feedback on their performance."},{"type":"p","text":"It can be helpful to develop a hiring plan to ensure that these standards continue to be evaluated and met, even years into the future. This will help keep your business fair and on track throughout its duration, even ten years down the line."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Value individual growth"},{"type":"p","text":"In 2014, Glassdoor found that 63% of employees want to learn new skills and train on the same because they consider it one of the most important factors for advancement. Coaching, mentoring and other developmental activities are extremely valued amongst employees as it shows your personal investment in them, which leads to mutual trust and respect."},{"type":"p","text":"Setting a culture of growth and productivity goes a long way because it gives employees the tools they need to perform well. You can guarantee that these methods work because theyll have already been vetted by employees who used those tools to find success themselves. Mentorship can come in many forms from having senior employees train new hires, offering regular training (and follow-up training sessions to brush up on their abilities), or bringing in industry professionals to host seminars and workshops on applicable pathways to success."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also try to encourage outside development in employees’ own time by playing on their desire for professional improvement, though this one is admittedly more difficult to sell. To foster career skills without monetary compensation, employees typically need other incentives, which also come in a variety forms. Team building is often a good place to start, because close bonds with coworkers breeds a better company culture and naturally makes team members want to try harder so as not to become a detriment to the group. Outside reward programs are also effective, such as offering prizes for top sellers in the group or hosting a dinner to show your appreciation for the best shift team. Creativity goes a long way here because it depends on the specific wants and values of the individuals you’re trying to motivate."},{"type":"p","text":"Typically, employees put in as much effort as they’re paid to care about. It’s harsh but true. Minimum wage employeesor sometimes less than minimum wage employees, since tipped workers can make as little as $2.13/hrjust won’t care much about professional development without proper incentive. Raises and benefits remain the best motivator out there."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Review, review, review"},{"type":"p","text":"Setting goals is meaningless without follow-through. Only 2% of employers give ongoing feedback to employees which is unhelpful because it doesn’t tell them whether they’re doing well on a regular enough basis; progress takes a really long time because they can only change their tactics or strengthen the approaches that work once or twice a year. Especially in an industry with turnover so high, most employees probably won’t even last to see a review."},{"type":"p","text":"Take that into consideration with the fact that most people dread yearly reviews, and it’s actually more beneficial to have more informal, frequent reviews. Focus on development, not evaluation, as that only leads to fear of judgement rather than centering on improvement which isn’t the same thing. Asking targeted questions will help to this end, such as, “How can I, as a manager, help you improve?” or “What are your goals and what tools do you need to reach them?” or “How has management helped or hindered your work and success?” This puts the power of self-improvement in their hands and helps you set goals together, while also teaching employees to determine their own areas of professional development that need improvementwhich is a skillset in itself, recognizing weakness and taking steps to do better."},{"type":"p","text":"Creating collaborative, frequent reviews breed happier, more productive and more successful employees."},{"type":"p","text":"Staff are one of the most important, if not the heart, of any restaurant. Respect and personal investment in their development are the keys to building a great staff who will have as much vested interest in giving back to a company who has put so much into helping them grow critical skillsets."},{"type":"p","text":"This is especially important during the COVID-19 pandemic, since you likely have more time to invest in cross-training your employees and building a stronger business in the future when the world reopens. All of this will hopefully lead to lower turnover rates and a more cohesive and agile staff, working together to make your restaurant the best it can be."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #Restaurants #SmallBusiness #Staffing"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_24e71d719812452bbe4a6ba367d65c68~mv2.jpeg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-22', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('orderos-the-future-of-online-ordering', 'orderOS: The Future of Online Ordering', 'Over the past several years, customers have gotten more comfortable with off-premising ordering options. Still, COVID-19 has caused an explosion of favor for takeout and delivery, the likes of which have never been seen...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Over the past several years, customers have gotten more comfortable with off-premising ordering options. Still, COVID-19 has caused an explosion of favor for takeout and delivery, the likes of which have never been seen before."},{"type":"p","text":"Even this far into the pandemic, we still see cases rise all over the country, and new safety regulations come out month to month to month. As a result, restaurants are still closing indoor dining options or just switching over to online platforms. New revenue streams might be just the revitalization that your restaurant needs. Takeout and delivery are undoubtedly here to stay: Affordable pricing and safety concerns have made online ordering a prevalent consumer trend, with many indicating that they plan to continue prioritizing takeout and delivery after the pandemic passes. There are other viruses out there, and considering sanitation and social distance is now, for better or worse, embedded into the modern social consciousness."},{"type":"p","text":"Contactless technology is making its way onto service floors throughout the industry simultaneously, as restaurateurs recognize the rising importance of convenient social distancing. At eatOS, we’ve developed orderOS: A personalized branded website and mobile app that restaurants like you can use to launch your online ordering platform without any of the usual commission fees you get with other third party services."},{"type":"h2","text":"orderOS and the Future of Off-Premise Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"When you sign up with eatOS, we give you complete control over your layout and menu to make business decisions that the most make sense for you. Managing your own system is a huge benefit: When you add curbside services, for example, you can take into account the layout of your restaurant and parking lot when figuring out how to make sure orders go to the right cars in line. You can also optimize your menu to promote best-selling dishes front and center or make sure that it loads conveniently and sensibly on mobile."},{"type":"p","text":"Our mobile and online ordering platforms integrate with your existing system, so sales data continues to update in real-time while incorporating off-premise orders. All tickets automatically go to the Point of Sale and Kitchen Display Screen so cooks can get started immediately on orders, shortening wait times and making much happier customers. This increases the likelihood that each one will want to come back for more."},{"type":"h2","text":"Why Do Customers Love orderOS?"},{"type":"p","text":"What do customers get out of orderOS? They’ll enjoy contactless payment options as well as a more convenient ordering experience. Online and mobile ordering give customers a chance to peruse the full menu and double-check their tickets, meaning increased order accuracy as less gets lost in translation because of human error. orderOS is equipped for easy modifications and add-ons, but checkout notes take it to the next level by giving customers control over the delivery experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Order tracking is also improved with orderOS. Customers can see their orders’ progress in the queue, and workers can give more accurate time estimates for meals and open tables alike."},{"type":"p","text":"We improve the experience even down to each individual transaction. COVID-19 has shown the abject necessity of contactless payment and delivery options; customers can pay at their leisure with self-service, without fear of spreading this deadly virus. eatOS devices are equipped for swipe, tap, near-field communication, and online payments, so customers have the choice to complete the transaction; however, they’re most comfortable doing it."},{"type":"p","text":"When you sign up with eatOS, you’ll see the benefits of a custom branded merchant app and a revitalized online ordering webpage. The future of foodservice is online and mobile: eatOS developed orderOS as the perfect companion to this new dining era."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #Delivery #OnlineOrdering #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant #FoodServiceTechnologybyeatOS"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_4c24bfa7fa78463e9c50b97927eefc6a~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-19', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-highlight-dig-food-group', 'Restaurant Highlight: Dig Food Group', 'Since Adam Eskin first opened Dig (formerly known as Dig Inn) in 2011, it’s grown into a multifaceted business endeavor that now spans multiple states and involves more than just restaurants. Dig began as a way to...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Since Adam Eskin first opened Dig (formerly known as Dig Inn) in 2011, it’s grown into a multifaceted business endeavor that now spans multiple states and involves more than just restaurants. Dig began as a way to provide healthy, locally-sourced meals to guests and simultaneously support family farms in the community. Now, however, Dig has locations in New York, Boston, Philadelphia, Rye Brook and Brooklyn, and they deliver across Manhattan and Williamsburg."},{"type":"p","text":"On top of building a successful chain of fast-casual restaurants, they’ve undertaken endeavors that necessitated the invention of Dig Food Group. This organization encompasses the restaurant chain as well as Dig Acres Farm, a 12-acre plot in Orange County where they produce their own food. This began as a means to understand more about their friends at the local farms."},{"type":"p","text":"To help people in need during the COVID-19 pandemic, Dig Food Group is also putting their considerable resources toward community relief efforts."},{"type":"h2","text":"Dig Acres Farm Box"},{"type":"p","text":"At Dig, they’re no stranger to community-supported agriculture (also known as CSA). In the summer of 2019, Dig Acres Farm partnered with FoodKick, a same-day fresh food delivery service, to test out using a farm box to get fresh, organic vegetables into the homes of those who needed it. They opened their restaurants for a similar reason, however the farm box allowed them to reach and help more families."},{"type":"p","text":"On March 28th, they relaunched what they’ve dubbed the Dig Acres Farm Box since this pandemic began. Their website describes its contents as “farm-fresh produce from friends of Dig Acres. Selection of 7 - 9 vegetables rotates every Saturday.” Due to the nature of their work, Dig Food Group has connections with many local farmers who, since restaurants all over have shut down, now have an excess of supplies. Many people need these ingredients right now but struggle to find them on grocery shelves. The Dig Acres Farm Box helps local farmers unload and receive compensation for their sudden excess of supplies, and connects them to consumers who need the produce."},{"type":"p","text":"They reopened the farm box for two reasons. Firstly, they recognized that many people rely on grocery delivery but cannot find an available time slot on any of the platforms designed for this service. Thus Dig Food Group decided to be that go-between. Secondly they had already planned to reinstate their farm box this coming summer; however, given the pressing nature of COVID-19 and the unpredictable situation that it has thrust many households into, Dig Food Group decided to open the box earlier than planned so that they could do their part supporting the community. They already had the necessary resources, know-how and systems in place, thus they could reinstitute the farm box when people really needed the supplies."},{"type":"p","text":"The farm box changes every Saturday. Dig Food Group works with their local suppliers to discover what farmers need to unload that week and then design the box accordingly. They list what’s inside underneath the “GET A BOX” button on their website so customers can decide exactly what they need and when they need it."},{"type":"p","text":"The box has already had a major impactful on local communities, so much so that, although they began the endeavor in New York, as of April 24th Dig Food Group announced plans to expand their efforts to cover Philadelphia and Boston as well. Already, farmers and farmers market delivery companies are reaching out to see if they can join the effort. In times like these, we can never extend enough helping hands."},{"type":"h2","text":"Dig Feeds"},{"type":"p","text":"Dig Feeds is another endeavor started by the Dig Food Group. During this crisis, some families need more than healthy ingredients; some also require meals to get them through these tough times. Thus, Dig Food Group launched Dig Feeds."},{"type":"p","text":"According to the website, Dig Feeds aims to “feed people in need during this crisis and beyond. Our farmers and chefs who usually turn vegetables into food for Dig restaurants donate thousands of meals to the people who need them most. 100% of all funds contributed will go to the sourcing, cooking and serving of meals through Dig Feeds.”"},{"type":"p","text":"People in need can request a meal delivery. Those with the means to do so also have the option to gift a meal to somebody else. Dig Feeds is working hard to accommodate all dietary restrictions and allergies to ensure that they can efficiently and effectively help as many people as possible."},{"type":"p","text":"Dig Feeds also launched their “buy a bowl, give a bowl” program to further assist the most vulnerable members of the community. For each order they receive, they also donate a meal to a local hospital, school, homeless shelter, nonprofit, small business or other partner organization in need."},{"type":"p","text":"Over the course of this pandemic,, the Dig Food Group has already donated nearly 100K meals to people in need."},{"type":"h2","text":"Looking toward the future"},{"type":"p","text":"Dig Food Group has worked tirelessly to support local farms and families struggling because of this virus and the strain it has put on people and businesses alike. They have no plans to slow their relief work while COVID-19 continues to threaten society, and in fact hope to support their local farms, practice community relief efforts and get healthy food on consumers’ tables long after the danger has passed."},{"type":"p","text":"Although previous to this pandemic, Dig Food Group’s focus lay in their restaurant chain and organic farm partners, they hope to continue learning about and implementing effective community outreach in the future. As Taylor Lanzet, a member of Dig Food Group, put it: Its not about going back to what we were before, but building a better food system moving forward."},{"type":"p","text":"#CommunityOutreachStrategies #Covid19Pandemic #FoodService #Restaurants"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_5bb8287330774fb893af79d19e5e2eac~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-17', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('a-safer-back-of-house', 'A Safer Back of House.', 'Commercial kitchens are the backbone of every restaurant, but the bustling busyness of the back of house leaves your workers open for potential injuries. From sharp knives to hot food spillage, kitchens are a hotbed of...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Commercial kitchens are the backbone of every restaurant, but the bustling busyness of the back of house leaves your workers open for potential injuries. From sharp knives to hot food spillage, kitchens are a hotbed of risks that cost employers both the financial strain of worker’s compensation and lost productivity once your back of house team is out-of-step."},{"type":"p","text":"When you streamline your kitchen to maximize safety and efficiency, you help staff avoid missing days that can cause them undue financial stress too. Many restaurant employees are hourly workers. Save everyone time and stress by improving in these five areas."},{"type":"h2","text":"Back of House Safety"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Appropriate Dress Code"},{"type":"p","text":"Although they don’t have to look spiffy in a uniform for customers’ benefit, it’s still crucial that kitchen staff follow dress code. That stereotypical outfit that comes into your head when you hear the word “chef” is a common consensus for a reason. Hats and hairnets prevent hair from getting singed or into the food. Close-toed shoes are necessary to avoid dropping heavy objects on the feet, while nonslip and waterproof shoes prevent discomfort if cooks step in something nasty so their minds can stay focused on the job."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Slip Prevention"},{"type":"p","text":"Spills are bound to happen in a commercial kitchen, whether it’s food that leaves floors sticky or water that causes people to slip. Consider buying mats for your commercial kitchen to reduce the risk of falling and injury on the job."},{"type":"p","text":"Signs help. Put up notices so people know when the floors are dirty, if there are extension cords to watch out for and any other hazards. Cordon off affected areas until someone can clean up the mess, although it’s best to encourage workers to tackle spills immediately."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Ventilation and Guards"},{"type":"p","text":"Commercial kitchen equipment needs to be treated with care to protect your back of house team. Equip proper ventilation to let out heat, smoke and smell so kitchen staff can work without interruptions or distractions. Clean vents are required to pass a health inspection anyway, so it’s best to tackle these tasks regularly."},{"type":"p","text":"Meanwhile other equipment should have the proper guards so your workers don’t injure themselves on the job. Food preparation can involve sharp, dangerous tools and high speed order turnaround, and this combination can lead to careless mistakes. Make sure nobody loses a finger when they’re hastily slicing the meat for the lunch rush."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Fire Preparedness Plan"},{"type":"p","text":"Grease fires are the most common type of fire that affects commercial kitchens, and it can’t be suppressed with your average sprinkler. Instead, equip a fire suppression system that automatically turns off the gas line when the alarm is tripped. Range hoods now come with fire suppressant spray to help minimize accidents."},{"type":"p","text":"In a panic, people will make mistakes and forget the procedures they’ve carefully learned. Staff should know and have easy access to extinguishers, blankets and the trigger for the suppression system. Give your staff fire safety training including basic first aid instruction for treating burns or administering CPR. Do evacuation drills so they know how to safely proceed in the event of an actual emergency."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. OSHA Compliance"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants need to be OSHA compliant to avoid health hazards and getting shut down by inspectors. Take a day to train staff on OSHA-approved ways to safely lift heavy objects, store and handle ingredients, prevent or reduce stress injuries, and generally remove potential hazards from around their workspaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Louis Hansel @shotsoflouis on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Future Success"},{"type":"p","text":"Reducing risks and hazards around a commercial kitchen requires some adjustment, and you might have to implement new systems to guarantee workers’ safety. Rigorous cleaning systems, for example, ensure a hygienic experience for customers but it’s also grown more important for employees as the COVID-19 threat necessitates social distance and increased sanitation on the job."},{"type":"p","text":"Incorporate these safety tips into your onboarding and orientation to give your staff the tools they need to work safer and smarter from the jump. Consider streamlining your operations and improving your output with superior restaurant technology."},{"type":"p","text":"#StaffingampRecruiting"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_404cb4ad80564a0098a9eb1d69a57494~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-16', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('how-vaccines-will-affect-online-ordering', 'How Vaccines Will Affect Online Ordering', 'The further we get into summer, the more Americans will be itching to get out of the house and back to normal. Over half of adults now have at least one shot, according to the New York Times, meaning full inoculation...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The further we get into summer, the more Americans will be itching to get out of the house and back to normal. Over half of adults now have at least one shot, according to the New York Times, meaning full inoculation will only become more commonplace. Widespread eligibility also means that all adults who want vaccines should have one this summer. Understandably, restaurants wonder whether this portends the end of online ordering."},{"type":"p","text":"Cytonn Photography on Unsplash"},{"type":"p","text":"Throughout the pandemic, restaurants have relied on off-premise ordering to survive. From takeout to delivery, customers adapted to new sales channels when dine-in services closed. Understandably, restaurants have concerns that more vaccinations will diminish online ordering sales. It would lay waste to all the effort they put in to fortify these platforms."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Is Online Ordering Headed?"},{"type":"p","text":"Although a lot of people will be able to dine out safely soon, without significant risk to themselves, there’s still a chance of spreading the infection to others. We’re creating a culture of normalized social distance and mask-wearing. That, alongside growing comfort with self-service options, has PYMNTS estimating that 92% of guests will continue their online ordering habits after inoculation."},{"type":"p","text":"This is great news for restaurants. Average ticket size increases when customers have the luxury of browsing the menu on their own time. This, alongside the customizations and auto-prompted modifications available with the orderOS app, encourage guests to add more to their plates. In addition to that, states are reopening at different rates. A lot still won’t offer full dine-in seating for a while. Customers will continue using online ordering because it’s where most restaurants still do business. If they want variety or don’t know what they’re craving, they’ll have to check their apps."},{"type":"h2","text":"Vaccines and Dine-In Service"},{"type":"p","text":"In states that allow it, some restaurants have opened their service floor to partial and even full capacity. This will happen with more regularity in the coming months, although vaccine rollouts are also happening at different rates depending on your state and city. The summer will likely bring vaccinations to every adult who wants it, but that doesn’t completely solve the problem of safely dining in. For starters, there are those who refuse to or can’t get vaccinated. For another, children still aren’t wildly eligible like adults."},{"type":"p","text":"The longer we go without herd immunity, the more variants of the virus have a chance to cause devastation. Social responsibility also plays a role, as guests consider staff’s safety too. They may not want to go out too often and have to make a judgment call about whether a restaurant visit is a more worthwhile trip than a family’s house. All in all, it’s safe to say dining in will return slowly rather than all at once."},{"type":"p","text":"Obi Onyeador on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Online Ordering and Vaccines, Together"},{"type":"p","text":"One thing’s for sure: People will start dining out more, even as online ordering remains a prevalent sales channel moving forward. They’ll likely start getting food delivered and going out to dinner more often with their friends, both fully vaccinated and not. Given that people still report wanting to order in after the pandemic ends, you might just see an uptick in traffic in both your online and in-person channels."},{"type":"p","text":"To meet whatever comes next, you need a smart Point of Sale system."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_33dcc6a700aa4f99850372f207b177df~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-12', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('10-best-california-cities-to-start-a-restaurant', '10 Best California Cities to Start a Restaurant', 'After more than a year, people finally feel comfortable enough to open new businesses again. As they open their doors this summer, owners are still looking for the best place to put down roots. From COVID-19 regulations...', '[{"type":"p","text":"After more than a year, people finally feel comfortable enough to open new businesses again. As they open their doors this summer, owners are still looking for the best place to put down roots. From COVID-19 regulations to whole new pools of customers, different cities have their own pros and cons. If you’re an entrepreneur looking at the west coast, here are the 10 best cities in California to start a new restaurant right now."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Robert Bye on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Where to Open a Restaurant in California"},{"type":"p","text":"With the state reopening, cities set their own jurisdiction about how closely to follow mask mandates and other rules. Within that, restaurants decide what’s best for them and their customers. Using 21 metrics, including available opportunities and your likelihood of success, one study found the hundred best places to open a restaurant. Out of those, we took the top ten in California to break down further."},{"type":"p","text":"01. Irvine. Ranking best in education out of these ten cities, opening here could mean recruiting more qualified applicants."},{"type":"p","text":"02. Long Beach. With the most human capital available, restaurants can cut down on those undefinable costs and interpersonal obstacles that make running a streamlined team such hard work."},{"type":"p","text":"03. Fresno"},{"type":"p","text":"04. Oakland"},{"type":"p","text":"05. Stockton. This Central Valley city boasts the cheapest average rent on the list. If you’re worried about keeping overhead costs low, then this may be the place for you."},{"type":"p","text":"06. Los Angeles. You can’t get a culture like L.A. anywhere else. If vibe and ambiance are your settings, maybe here will attract your ideal clientele."},{"type":"p","text":"07. San Diego"},{"type":"p","text":"08. San Francisco. Up north, SF is the place to be for higher-end restaurants and owners looking for a different kind of culture. The NoCal city also has the second-highest educated workforce on the list, after Irvine."},{"type":"p","text":"09. Sacramento"},{"type":"p","text":"10. San Bernardino. Employees here have the shortest workweek on average. Time off gives them a chance to mentally reset between shifts, so this could actually net better productivity and retention. Plus, it’s a good selling point for recruiting new hires and ethically-minded customers."},{"type":"p","text":"Where you settle down depends on what you prioritize. Do you prefer the low cost of operations? Or maybe a certain demographic of customers, or perhaps a big-spending clientele? Take into consideration what each city has to offer, and then decide what’s best for your specific business."},{"type":"h2","text":"Building a Business that Thrives"},{"type":"p","text":"Although these ten cities are the top candidates based on a myriad of factors, that doesn’t mean you can’t succeed elsewhere. It also doesn’t mean that anyone choice is worse than another. Different businesses will benefit from different priorities in the long term. Most likely, you won’t be able to get the best of every feature but you can control those which matter most to the brand and its customers."},{"type":"p","text":"For the most streamlined and successful opening, equip your restaurant with cutting-edge technology. Draw in and retain guests, cut down on operating and labor expenses, and organize your workforce right away by investing in a smart Point of Sale system."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #CaliforniaRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_59118724ba6748b6bdf614b25d6ec7cc~mv2.jpg', 'Inventory Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-11', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('3-clever-solutions-to-the-labor-shortage', '3 Clever Solutions to the Labor Shortage', 'As the pandemic winds down for summer, all kinds of businesses have had trouble hiring back who they laid off in 2020. Restaurants in particular feel the strain. Job openings rose by tens of thousands just since this...', '[{"type":"p","text":"As the pandemic winds down for summer, all kinds of businesses have had trouble hiring back who they laid off in 2020. Restaurants in particular feel the strain. Job openings rose by tens of thousands just since this year began, so managers that want to entice back hesitant workers need to find new solutions. Answers to the labor shortage come in unexpected places."},{"type":"p","text":"For starters, the most influential factor when choosing where to work will be whether or not they pay a living wage. Workers have been hit just as hard as businesses, financially. Expanded unemployment benefits that equal more than a full-time job just doesn’t add up. Therefore, some restaurants have made working there more appealing. Consider:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Pay bumps by several dollars an hour"},{"type":"p","text":"2. Hourly bonuses for holidays, or the entire summer"},{"type":"p","text":"3. Signing and referral bonuses, and then extra bonuses per quarter based on performance"},{"type":"p","text":"4. Flexible schedules, and even make-your-own hours depending on the position"},{"type":"p","text":"Find creative solutions that work for your business. Ultimately, workers just want adequate compensation and job satisfaction. If you can offer them that, they’re much more likely to come work for you over your competition."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"h2","text":"Effective New Workplaces"},{"type":"p","text":"It’s not just about what you can offer them, but what kind of environment your restaurant cultivates. Good pay won’t overcome poor working conditions. Internal changes may be called for. For example, maybe you’re typically open 24/7. With limited workers, you might have to cut down availability so you can have a full staff when you are open."},{"type":"p","text":"For others, hire help by relaxing certain requirements. Perhaps implement an all-new pay structure that allows people without certain qualifications a chance for upwards growth. This is also an opportunity for them to train under their coworkers, and it shows them they can reach better paying positions with more responsibility. Just remember that everyone needs a living wage, even if they don’t have a masters degree."},{"type":"h2","text":"Long-Term Foundations for Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"This labor shortage is indicative of the change coming for the hospitality industry, and American businesses as a whole. It won’t be solved with a few months of better working conditions before things revert back to how they were before. When encouraging more applicants, consider what will have long-term effects on recruitment and retention. For example, good company culture goes a long way. When they work with friends and feel valued by employers, staff members are more likely to give the position their all."},{"type":"p","text":"Or maybe you provide benefits they can’t get elsewhere, like health insurance or childcare. Do you offer PTO so they can go get vaccinated? These things matter more than ever to potential workers, and their concerns aren’t going away. The labor shortage isn’t from a lack of people looking for jobs; it’s a simple matter of supply not meeting demand. What is your restaurant doing to sway the market in your favor?"},{"type":"p","text":"If you need to cut down on labor costs and streamline operations while onboarding new workers, you need a smart Point of Sale system. The right restaurant technology makes running your business cheaper, easier and more effective than ever before."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #Covid19Pandemic #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant #WorkforceManagement"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_57d8de9cf9f44c41907b5111816efb43~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-09', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('5-reasons-why-you-need-a-kitchen-display-system', '5 Reasons Why You Need a Kitchen Display System', 'It’s the least-seen part of your restaurant, but serves one of the most essential functions: The kitchen, where the real action is. Considering how big a role the back-of-house plays in your operations, it’s critical to...', '[{"type":"p","text":"It’s the least-seen part of your restaurant, but serves one of the most essential functions: The kitchen, where the real action is. Considering how big a role the back-of-house plays in your operations, it’s critical to equip them with the most cutting-edge technology to make their job run as smoothly as possible."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS developed a Kitchen Display System (KDS) to help make your kitchen better. When your staff can get order information right away, they can begin cooking faster, reduce wait times, and improve overall satisfaction levels. Once you integrate KDS into your daily operations, you’ll wonder how you ever worked any other way."},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Order Accuracy"},{"type":"p","text":"Technology ensures that customers get exactly what they want without mistakes or long wait times. Orders on paper tickets can get lost in translation due to accidents or human error; whether because of messy handwriting, smudging, damage or simply because the ticket gets lost in the back-of-house chaos, KDS are easier to read and manage. Improve the accuracy of every order so that no customer has an underwhelming experience because of a game of telephone."},{"type":"p","text":"Eliminating paper tickets is better for the environment, too. Reduce your paper waste while improving your restaurant operations with KDS. When paired with other self-service devices, orders are even more accurate because they come right from the customers fingertips."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Streamline Cooking Process"},{"type":"p","text":"The kitchen is one of the busiest places in your restaurant; the work is nonstop. KDS makes it easy to consolidate items and formalize the cooking process a little more, which helps your staff stay on task. For example, if six different customers want a side of fries, that station will be able to see it on the screen and make a big batch of fries at once. This reduces the time that customers have to wait for their orders and makes preparation less stressful for your employees, too."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Track Order Fulfillment"},{"type":"p","text":"KDS track fulfillment times to give you a better idea of the speed and efficiency of your kitchen. Re-prioritize orders, separate items to their correct station and monitor how long orders take to fill so you can eliminate unnecessary delays and better streamline your overall operations. Tracking capabilities make employees’ jobs more straightforward and organized, while also resulting in happier customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Inventory Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Auto-generated reports will analyze your data in real time to help you monitor everything that goes on in your kitchen. Track your inventory levels and order volumes, and even enable auto-alerts so you know when you’re low on any item. Never run out of supplies or let food go to waste, optimize your kitchen efficiency, and reduce pointless spending."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Table Turns"},{"type":"p","text":"When your operation is streamlined to maximum efficiency, and you’ve reduced wait times thanks to automation and technology, the entire dine-in process speeds up from start to finish. This means that table turn timehow long customers spend at your establishment from ordering to paymenthastens too, so you seat more customers throughout the day and improve profits accordingly. Patrons appreciate faster service and leave more satisfied with their experience, too. With KDS, you have a better chance of making each guest a loyal one."},{"type":"p","text":"Real-time data, cross-channel consistency, and streamlined back of house efficiency are all made possible with KDS and other cutting-edge restaurant technology solutions. Better customer service and improved operations means that you can handle more sales, encourage greater customer satisfaction and loyalty, and pad your bottom line so you have a more successful, more efficient restaurant that you can be proud of."},{"type":"p","text":"Kitchen Display Systems are proven to help restaurants of all sizes. Schedule a demo with eatOS today to find out what makes our KDS outshine. For any restaurant, big or small, eatOS’S KDS can help them all."},{"type":"p","text":"#RestaurantTechnologyandCOVID19 #eatOS #CloudKitchens #kitchendisplay #RestaurantBusiness"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_778cdb868abb4ae39e66dad6e51dc2b7~mv2.jpeg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-08', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('5-tips-for-safe-restaurant-reopening', '5 Tips for Safe Restaurant Reopening', 'After over a year of rigid COVID-19 regulations and a global pandemic that touched every aspect of modern life, we’re finally seeing a light at the end of the tunnel. As vaccines roll out and the service industry is...', '[{"type":"p","text":"After over a year of rigid COVID-19 regulations and a global pandemic that touched every aspect of modern life, we’re finally seeing a light at the end of the tunnel. As vaccines roll out and the service industry is reopening at greater capacities, restaurants look forward to safely returning to business as usual."},{"type":"p","text":"little plant on Unsplash"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants can follow these 5 tips to keep everybody safe as we move past this pandemic together."},{"type":"h2","text":"Safely Reopening After COVID-19"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Prioritize Sanitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Now, people have grown accustomed to seeing intense cleaning processes to disinfect spaces between guests. Make sure to pay attention to these concerns. Have an effective ventilation system so as to circulate clean air, continue temperature screenings for people who come inside and check in with employees to remind them to self-monitor. If you offer single-use masks and somewhere to store their mask while eating, this also shows you’re willing to go the extra mile."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Communicate with Guests"},{"type":"p","text":"As we begin to heal from the pandemic, customers retain the fears they rightfully developed this year. They want to know what’s going on so they can make informed decisions about their own safety. Honesty and transparency will have them returning, trustful, to dine with you again. Things will likely change as rapidly as they did last year, so stay on top of updates across your social channels that have the most engagement."},{"type":"p","text":"Update your marketing techniques to reflect the appropriate tone, too. If people need empathy, hope or a dose of reality, lean into that feeling. Your social media and promotional deals post-pandemic won’t look the same as they did when we were in the thick of things."},{"type":"p","text":"Fortunately, direction communication is a little bit easier because of contact tracing. Restaurants are already making customer profiles with names, numbers, emails and sales data on each guest. When you’re collecting information, take the opportunity to ask if they’d like to sign up for your email newsletter. Improve your marketing with all of this collected sales data and send deals made just for them, straight to their inbox."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Develop Emergency Procedures"},{"type":"p","text":"This past year has shown that we need to be ready for anything. Coronavirus-related emergencies will likely continue to crop up throughout the recovery period. Thus it’s good to plan in advance and create procedures for different situations that might occur. What should staff do in the event of an outbreak or if someone tests positive? They need to know this before an emergency occurs while they’re unprepared."},{"type":"p","text":"Have written procedures with your expectations about returning to work, too. If you expect regular hand washing or tasks to be handled in a certain way, a reopening guide reassures your employees regarding what to do. They can refer back to these procedures if they forget their training under pressure."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Have Your Workers’ Backs"},{"type":"p","text":"Your employees have kept business running this past year and will ensure its success going forward. Give them the respect and dedication they’ve shown you, by providing vaccination accommodations such as days off afterward to recover from the side effects. PTO, hazard pay and benefits also speak directly to the financial and safety hardships the service industry has experienced this past year. Supporting their health and showing that you care inspires your employees to give back in the form of motivation and providing a better customer experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Technology that Paves the Way"},{"type":"p","text":"Between getting used to it during the pandemic and realizing the added convenience of self-ordering via mobile app or Self-Service Kiosk, this trend is projected to continue long after we’ve fully returned to normal, unrestricted life. Contactless technology, for example, eases any remaining concerns about meeting strangers, so it’s likely that devices and updates will grow around these preferences. Even dine-in service is getting more touch-free these days."},{"type":"p","text":"Fábio Alves on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"More Reopening Resources"},{"type":"p","text":"Reputable organizations have come out with guidelines for safely reopening restaurants during and after COVID-19."},{"type":"p","text":"1. The National Restaurant Association, known commonly as the other NRA, has a reopening guide for the industry."},{"type":"p","text":"2. The CDC compiled tips for restaurants and bars looking to get back to work."},{"type":"p","text":"3. The FDA wrote a checklist in the summer of 2020 whose advice remains relevant now."},{"type":"p","text":"Use these COVID-19 health and safety recommendations to boost confidence that your restaurant is a safe place to eat."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #CoronavirusPandemic #Covid19Pandemic #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_8f10223fd70340bcb6ba2dc12ec0c5e4~mv2.jpg', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-04', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('after-covid-19-online-ordering-still-grows', 'After COVID-19, Online Ordering Still Grows', 'Restaurants around the country opened this summer after more than a year of pandemic-related complications. To adapt, many opened contactless dining options. Delivery was by far the most popular option, as it was a...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants around the country opened this summer after more than a year of pandemic-related complications. To adapt, many opened contactless dining options. Delivery was by far the most popular option, as it was a convenient way for guests and restaurants to safely continue doing business together. Yet despite service floors reopening to sit-down customers, online ordering continues to flourish. Why is that?"},{"type":"p","text":"The obvious benefits of food delivery caused many people to predict that its prevalence would remain as the danger waned. Throughout 2020, people became very comfortable using their phones to get their favorite meals delivered, ready and fresh, to their doors. Meanwhile it’s still an effective sales channel as long as you have the right tools for a cost-effective system. Starting takeout channels can involve a lot of time and money depending on what you have to work with."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"h2","text":"Online Ordering Systems Grow"},{"type":"p","text":"Takeout also enjoyed, and continue to experience, favor in the restaurant community. New services launch all the time. Why? It’s a faster way for restaurants to get online and start making money, so plenty are clamoring for an online ordering system that fits their needs."},{"type":"p","text":"It’s not all third party platforms like Uber Eats, either. Consider eatOS Point of Sale, for example. We created orderOS to take mobile orders from your customers on a branded app made just for you. That comes with:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. no third party commission fees."},{"type":"p","text":"2. seamless integration into your existing POS system."},{"type":"p","text":"3. cloud connectivity for instantaneous communication with the back of house."},{"type":"p","text":"4. menu syncing to automatically send updates to the whole store at once."},{"type":"p","text":"5. a focus on customer loyalty by providing features like notifications when their order is ready, delivery tracking and more."},{"type":"p","text":"Given that these are beneficial capabilities with or without the pandemic, people aren’t giving up on online ordering yet."},{"type":"h2","text":"Will This Trend Continue?"},{"type":"p","text":"At least in some places, COVID-19 is getting worse, not better. Mask mandates are going back into effect in places like California. Meanwhile, the Delta variant is a growing threat to health and safety. Cases are rising in a lot of places with a plethora of unvaccinated residents. Not only is COVID-19 not over, but it could be coming back again."},{"type":"p","text":"Thus the online ordering industry won’t grow as quickly anymore, but it is still growing. Habits developed during the pandemic are now integral aspects of a positive guest experience. Some have even seeped into dine-in service. For example, eatOS has QR Code ordering that lets customers scan the code at the table to bring up a mobile menu. Then they can order and pay from their phones. Clearly, though online ordering may not be as ubiquitous as it was during the height of the pandemic since people are excited to go out again, it will remain a very popular option, particularly for younger generations."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Beth Macdonald on Unsplash"},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #Covid19Pandemic #OnlineOrdering #RestaurantBusiness #FoodDelivery #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_5a2bd5be51b84bfbb762fba5132a2807~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-03', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('american-rescue-plan-to-restaurants-aid', 'American Rescue Plan to Restaurants’ Aid', 'Recently, the U.S. passed a $1.9T stimulus to get the country back on its feet. Most restaurants still struggle to bring in as much business as before. The economy will also need a boost to convince Americans, who have...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Recently, the U.S. passed a $1.9T stimulus to get the country back on its feet. Most restaurants still struggle to bring in as much business as before. The economy will also need a boost to convince Americans, who have had significant financial difficulties this year, to spend more money dining out even after we see the other side of this. That’s what the American Rescue Plan intends to do."},{"type":"p","text":"The stimulus sets aside $28.5B for the Restaurant Revitalization Fund. The Small Business Administration will distribute grants to those small businesses hit the hardest by COVID-19. This past year, restaurant sales fell by hundreds of billions of dollars and 110K restaurants closed forever. The American Rescue Plan is the first step toward widespread industry recovery."},{"type":"h2","text":"What does the ARP do?"},{"type":"p","text":"When the plan got signed, the National Restaurant Association disseminated information about what it is and why it’s important. This stimulus package gives restaurants much-needed tools to make future investments or restock on needed assets and inventory so they’re ready to meet the post-pandemic world with open arms."},{"type":"p","text":"This is the second and more productive stimulus plan for restaurants. PPP loans distributed last year insufficiently covered the industry, thus so many restaurants closed because they couldn’t pay their workers, rent, and other expenses. This new stimulus aims to guide them through the final stages of the pandemic until enough people get vaccinated, and states relax their capacity restrictions, for them to make revenue through sit-down service again. As we enter the recovery stage, restaurants are eager to keep their doors open through the home stretch."},{"type":"h2","text":"How can restaurants spend the money?"},{"type":"p","text":"Of the $5B earmarked for small businesses, the rest will be distributed to different-sized restaurants based on annual income. They define “small business” as those who make less than $500K annually in gross revenue."},{"type":"p","text":"The package covers restaurant expenses made between February 15, 2020, through the end of this year. It covers rent, utilities, PPE, sick leave, payroll for certain employees, operational and supplier costs, food and beverage expenses, building an outdoor seating space, maintenance repairs, and other critical purchases that independent restaurants need to stay open and successful."},{"type":"p","text":"Note that lately, Americans have pushed for higher wages, greater benefits, and better working conditions for low-income workers. Although the proposed $15/hr minimum wage didn’t pass Congress, the proposition nevertheless demonstrates that it’s a prevalent concern. It will be good to have money set aside in these grants for payroll, even just the usual payroll expenses, when sit-down service returns in force with a full staff hard at work."},{"type":"p","text":"Syed Ahmad on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"Through COVID-19 and beyond"},{"type":"p","text":"The future remains precarious between evolving restrictions, loosening safety regulations, vaccine rollout, and the virus itself developing new strains. The Restaurant Revitalization Fund part of the American Rescue Plan aims to reduce some of the uncertainty and get the foodservice industry through the rest of the year."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #CoronavirusPandemic #Covid19Pandemic #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_7a97c347a48d46ed89b5e13115b650aa~mv2.jpg', 'Inventory Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-05-01', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('check-out-retailnow-this-july', 'Check Out RetailNOW This July', 'Restaurants are excited to get back up and running this summer, and so are businesses adjacent to foodservice. Whether you run a restaurant or provide the technology for them, reconnect with the industry this July at...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants are excited to get back up and running this summer, and so are businesses adjacent to foodservice. Whether you run a restaurant or provide the technology for them, reconnect with the industry this July at the RetailNOW show."},{"type":"p","text":"Why? Because the industry is emerging from the COVID-19 pandemic very different from how it went in. Everyone could use networking opportunities, new partners, and the latest technology to get back on their feet. The RetailNOW show is a great place to learn more."},{"type":"p","text":"WHERE? Nashville, TN at Gaylord Opryland Events Center"},{"type":"p","text":"WHEN? July 25th through July 27"},{"type":"p","text":"If you’re interested in learning more about the restaurant industry, upcoming trends, marketing, online services, and payment systems, then check out this event at the end of July. There’s something new and interesting for everyone."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by RODNAE Productions from Pexels"},{"type":"h2","text":"The RetailNOW 2021 Show"},{"type":"p","text":"Their website marks the event as, “The retail IT channel’s trade show, education conference, and networking event is back - bigger and better than ever!”"},{"type":"p","text":"It’s true; you can get all sorts of things out of the event depending on what you’re looking for. With hundreds of booths, you’ll find all sorts of information pertinent to your business."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Educational information that affects the core functions of your restaurant, for the better."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Industry experts talking about how they handle various aspects of modern restaurant ownership. From ghost kitchens to cloud technology and everything in between, staying up-to-date on the latest industry trends keeps you in competition with the best."},{"type":"p","text":"3. Meet other vendors to form partnerships and networking opportunities. Support systems will be important during the recovery period post-COVID. This also presents an opportunity to run joint promotions or events with other vendors."},{"type":"p","text":"4. Recognizing both up-and-comers to the industry and superstars who are setting the bar for great leadership."},{"type":"p","text":"This year the RPSA will present Vendor Awards of Excellence. Resellers vote for prominent members of the retail technology industry to honor their hard work, particularly VARs (Value-Added Resellers) and ISVs (Independent Software Vendors) trendsetting for the industry at large."},{"type":"h2","text":"Join eatOS This July"},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS will see you at booth. Sign up as an attendee or open a booth, and come say hi at the event!"},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #Restaurant #RestaurantBusiness"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_a2d59c0386814d93a595c70cf6cefda0~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-28', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('eatos-partners-at-the-retailnow-show-in-nashville', 'eatOS Partners at the RetailNOW Show in Nashville', 'Are you ready for the RetailNOW 2021 show? This weekend, July 25th through July 27th, resellers will gather in Nashville, TN for the industry event of the summer. eatOS has their booth and is ready to meet with other...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Are you ready for the RetailNOW 2021 show? This weekend, July 25th through July 27th, resellers will gather in Nashville, TN for the industry event of the summer. eatOS has their booth and is ready to meet with other industry professionals, restaurant representatives who want to know more about what we do here, and anyone else who wants to stop by and say hi!"},{"type":"p","text":"The event takes place at the Gaylord Opryland Events Center. eatOS is proud to join some of our merchant partners at the event."},{"type":"h2","text":"eatOS Partners and RSPA"},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Emma Dau on Unsplash"},{"type":"p","text":"The Retail Solutions Providers Association, more commonly known as RSPA, hosts the RetailNOW show each year. Some of our outstanding merchant partners even sponsor the organization! We’re proud to work with Blue Star, a platinum sponsor; Ingenico Group and Star Micronics, both silver sponsors; Epson, a bronze sponsor; and so many other great companies."},{"type":"p","text":"Meet us and our outstanding partners at the event this upcoming weekend. Check out our booths, keynote speakers sharing their industry expertise, new networking connections, the latest products sweeping the marketplace, and so much more that will help any business flourish."},{"type":"p","text":"Star Micronics will also host a podcast at the trade show, and you can expect to hear a special guest from our very own eatOS team, so be sure to tune in!"},{"type":"h2","text":"See You at RetailNOW 2021!"},{"type":"p","text":"Expect to see hundreds of first-time attendees, companies, and countries all around the world represented at this year’s show. Especially with people excited to get out and rejoin the business world after over a year, people are excited to network at the event, even more than any other reason for attending."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS is ready to meet partners, professionals and prospective new relationships at the RetailNOW show in Nashville this coming weekend. We’ll also be debuting our new eatOS Point of Purchase at the event, so be sure to stop by booth and see our latest restaurant POS device!"},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RetailNOW #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_5199d8c7ecb34250993c773d32247324~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Insights', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-26', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('healthy-food-trends-to-expect-this-summer', 'Healthy Food Trends to Expect This Summer', 'The COVID-19 pandemic has caused a massive shift in how Americans dine out. Newfound concerns center on health and wellness, especially when it comes to what we consume. That’s why sales have risen for foods that do...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The COVID-19 pandemic has caused a massive shift in how Americans dine out. Newfound concerns center on health and wellness, especially when it comes to what we consume. That’s why sales have risen for foods that do something for our bodies. Whether they improve mental health, boost energy, or boost the immune system and digestive health, people want to nourish themselves. This is especially true while fear lingers about a dangerous respiratory virus. That’s why probiotic food and drinks are selling more as well, like kombucha, yogurt, and kefir. Healthy food is getting more popular."},{"type":"p","text":"But it’s not just that. More Americans started diets in 2020, too. According to the International Food Information Council, 43% were on diets last year. That beats the few years previous, possibly as part of the wave of people expanding their horizons during quarantine. Dietary-restricted menus draw in people who follow vegan, vegetarian, gluten-free, keto, or paleo diets, to name just a few with waves of new followers."},{"type":"p","text":"Plant-based menus are also on the rise. Tofu, grains, chickpeas, and similar foods are replacing ingredients in popular dishes. For example, trade beef for beans in that burger, and your new target audience will follow. These alternatives aren’t just good for business and customers’ health; they’re good for the planet, too."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by amoon ra on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"What Restaurants Can Do"},{"type":"p","text":"Even if they don’t end up ordering the healthy option, customers like to know it’s on the menu anyway. According to a 2019 Technomic study, 34% of diners would prefer a restaurant just because of its healthy options."},{"type":"p","text":"It doesn’t have to be as complicated as overhauling the whole menu. You can offer ingredient alternatives to appease customers and keep costs down. Have a list of non-meat burgers or gluten-free buns. Milk alternatives have multiplied too, like coconut, almond, and soy. Swapping out ingredients is a simple way to fulfill this rising expectation amongst consumers."},{"type":"p","text":"Even just offering healthy side options works, too. You don’t have to exclusively pare down the menu to healthy food choices in order to effectively draw in those new customers. Keep that side of fries and onion fries, and just add grilled veggies or soup as another."},{"type":"h2","text":"Healthy Food Trends This Summer"},{"type":"p","text":"In the coming months, the warm weather will keep driving people to try those in-season fruits and vegetables. That will coincide with the rise in digital ordering, like takeout and delivery via QR code or a branded app. For the best restaurant experience, you need a smart and efficient Point of Sale system."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS offers an all-in-one cloud-based eco-system exclusively for restaurants. From Point of Sale to Contactless Ordering, Pay & Order at Table, Kitchen Display System, Guest Facing Display, Online Ordering APP / Website and Workforce Management there is everything to help a restaurant succeed no matter the size. Click Here to Schedule a demo to learn more about how your restaurant can make a smooth transition into the world of restaurant technology made simple."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_32140846756843ea9e6adc08f7c28baf~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Growth', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-25', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('how-to-support-black-owned-businesses-nationwide', 'How to Support Black-Owned Businesses Nationwide', 'As peaceful protests over the death of George Floyd and against police brutality flourish around the country, many people want to find additional ways to support people of color in their communities. Some protest,...', '[{"type":"p","text":"As peaceful protests over the death of George Floyd and against police brutality flourish around the country, many people want to find additional ways to support people of color in their communities. Some protest, others donate, many share information and petitions, but people are also furthering community goals by supporting black-owned businesses in their area."},{"type":"p","text":"Black-owned companies are some of the ones hit hardest by the COVID-19 pandemic which has ravaged the U.S. for months, and they continue to struggle as partial reopening leaves nonessential businesses like restaurants operating at only partial capacity. Since the beginning of June, people have started looking for new ways to support black-owned initiatives in their communities."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lists of Black-Owned Businesses"},{"type":"p","text":"Resources for black-owned businesses as well as compilations of local, black-owned restaurants tailored for cities all across the country are appearing all over social media. With these on hand, people can use their takeout and delivery services while sheltering in place against COVID-19. Some of these lists cover broad areas, including restaurants across an entire state, whereas others stay specific to certain cities or smaller communities, and these circulate more locally."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Los Angeles"},{"type":"p","text":"This list of Los Angeles-based, black-owned restaurants has a plethora of information on each one so that people can easily find whatever will fill their cravings. The information provided includes which neighborhood the restaurant operates out of, their phone numbers and websites, social media, any gift cards and merchandise you can purchase, and of course the type of cuisine they serve there."},{"type":"p","text":"They cover all kinds of restaurants including barbecue, breakfast, vegan and vegetarian, Jamaican, seafood, soul food and more."},{"type":"p","text":"1. New York"},{"type":"p","text":"New Yorkers have made a variety of lists, all catering to different communities. This list covers over 200 restaurants all over New York City, while this one specifies the ones in Queens. Black-Owned Brooklyn runs an Instagram that highlights people, places and products throughout Brooklyn; they also have a website where you can subscribe to get more updates on the community as a whole."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Atlanta"},{"type":"p","text":"This guide compiled by Atlanta Beltline Hates You displays the neighborhoods, addresses, owners, Instagrams and websites of over one hundred black-owned restaurants in Atlanta, GA. They also include a list of other resources, a Google Maps sheet to direct community members straight to their restaurant of choice, and even have a submission form so Atlantans can help the creator expand the list."},{"type":"p","text":"1. D.C."},{"type":"p","text":"Black food writer and advocate Anela Malik curated black-owned restaurants in the DMV, also known as the Washington Metropolitan Area that includes D.C. as well as parts of Maryland, Virginia and West Virginia. A stand-out aspect of this particular list is that it specifically focuses on restaurants open now during COVID-19. Malik frequently updates the information to guarantee its continued relevance and accuracy."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Denver"},{"type":"p","text":"303 Magazine crafted a list of nearly 300 black-owned businesses in and around the Denver area. They don’t just name restaurants but also include companies across a variety of industries, as well as other resources that support the black community in Denver."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Louisville"},{"type":"p","text":"This blog operated by members of the Yelp Louisville Elite Squad not only names but reviews the best black-owned restaurants and food businesses in Kentucky. People have to apply to join the group, ensuring that top quality reviewers recommend the best of the best."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Minnesota"},{"type":"p","text":"Back where these protests started, Minnesotans are compiling black-owned restaurants and bars in the state. Along with this, they urge consumers to patronize these businesses all year long, not just during Black History Month or when there’s a large amount of civil unrest. Additionally, they’re asking readers to reach out and let them know about more businesses to supplement and bolster their list."},{"type":"p","text":"All around the U.S., people are making catalogues like these. Check out more cities who have compiled black-owned businesses in their communities including Austin, TX; Chicago, IL; New Jersey; Portland, OR; Seattle, WA and more. People want to support black-owned businesses, which is why these lists and many more like them are being created and shared across all different social media sites."},{"type":"p","text":"Order from these businesses, promote them on your own platforms and share these lists with your friends and neighbors. Generating extra business for black-owned restaurants is an easy way to support local community members and try new, great food in your neighborhood."},{"type":"h2","text":"Download Directories"},{"type":"p","text":"As support for black-owned restaurants rises en masse, so does loyalty to initiatives that help people find and order from them. Unlike community-organized lists, these are often apps that assemble local black-owned businesses, update regularly, and let people find and order food directly from their mobile device."},{"type":"p","text":"A few different directory-style apps have launched over the years, all sharing the same goal of promoting small, black-owned businesses around the country."},{"type":"p","text":"1. EatOkra"},{"type":"p","text":"This black-owned business directory app started because the founders wanted to give back to their community in a substantial way. As they put it, “Nothing embodies this idea of community more than the act of feeding someone or coming together to eat or be fed” which is why they’re constantly growing and maintaining their directory to help restaurants and community members flourish and get their needs met together."},{"type":"p","text":"1. The Black Wallet"},{"type":"p","text":"At The Black Wallet, they seek to uplift black entrepreneurs by promoting all types of businesses, their owners and the greater black community. Their efforts don’t end with their app and online directory: They also detail all of their services and offer educational courses that teach young entrepreneurs the skills they need to succeed."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Black Nation"},{"type":"p","text":"This business discovery app supports all kinds of black-owned businesses and entrepreneurs. Business owners can download the app and become featured for a chance to support and promote their company. Black Nation also has an Instagram where they promote businesses and important causes."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Support Black Owned"},{"type":"p","text":"This blog directory compiled black-owned businesses from all over the world so that people in every country can help support black entrepreneurs in their communities. They accept donations, offer great deals and feature businesses on their website. They also have an app that anyone can download and easily find nearby restaurants. Help take the movement worldwide with Support Black Owned."},{"type":"p","text":"These are just a few of the many directory apps coming to help support black-owned businesses in local communities. Since June began and the push to support black-owned businesses has grown in fervor, these apps and others like them have seen spikes in downloads anywhere from 50% to over 4000%."},{"type":"p","text":"On top of helping support black business owners, young entrepreneurs can also find resources to guide them to success."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Food Education Fund"},{"type":"p","text":"They have job training, paid internships and other entrepreneurship and enrichment programs that help prepare black high schoolers for a career in the food service industry."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Black and Brown Founders"},{"type":"p","text":"This initiative provides community, education and access to black and Latinx entrepreneurs. They supply them with resources that will help them succeed."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Black Female Founders"},{"type":"p","text":"They foster entrepreneurship and invention by providing business owners with the resources and information necessary to succeed."},{"type":"p","text":"1. Okra Academy"},{"type":"p","text":"A subset of The Okra Project, Okra Academy teaches kitchen basics and recipes to black trans people so they can enrich their personal lives in the kitchen. They also train to become better chefs so they can pursue a career in the food service industry, and the Project even provides homecooked meals to those in the black trans community who need it."},{"type":"p","text":"While these resources and programs spread through social media, news outlets like Forbes and Glamour are also promoting black-owned businesses and endeavors like these all around the country. Especially considering the mass pandemic affecting the entire world, independent restaurants all need community support."},{"type":"p","text":"Support black business owners by donating to and ordering directly from local restaurants. Whether compiled by community members on a Google doc or assembled in an app, you can support these local businesses easily just by ordering dinner."},{"type":"h2","text":"Today, Tomorrow and Every Day Beyond"},{"type":"p","text":"Supporting black lives shouldn’t end when the protests do. Don’t only shop at these restaurants because Black Lives Matter is trending. Instead, use these resources to get into the habit of supporting black-owned businesses and continue doing so long after this particular movement goes dormant."},{"type":"p","text":"Combatting systemic racism is an everyday process. Doing something as simple as shifting, at least partially, from patronizing chain establishments to supporting independently owned businesses, specifically black-owned independent businesses, is a very easy adjustment in your day to day life. Support people of color in your community, particularly black business owners working hard to serve their neighbors in the midst of protests for their right to live and the COVID-19 pandemic on top of that. The fight doesn’t end herebut it’s a good place to start."},{"type":"p","text":"#Community #FoodService"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_adee9251f7cb4ddb87876f8b2a96f527~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-21', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('meet-the-eatos-pop-at-retailnow-2021', 'Meet the eatOS POP at RetailNOW 2021', 'The RetailNOW Show is happening right now in Nashville. It began yesterday on July 25th and will continue on through tomorrow. eatOS is excited to have a booth set up there to connect with other industry...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The RetailNOW Show is happening right now in Nashville. It began yesterday on July 25th and will continue on through tomorrow. eatOS is excited to have a booth set up there to connect with other industry representatives, learn from experts and do so much more. We’re also introducing eatOS POP."},{"type":"p","text":"Image by Julia Schwab from Pixabay"},{"type":"h2","text":"Introducing eatOS POP, Out Now!"},{"type":"p","text":"This tradeshow will be the debut of our new device. POP, or Point of Purchase, is a handheld device with all the same functionality of a full-size Point of Sale. Servers can use its portability to offer tableside service to guests. It also connects to the rest of your restaurant system so orders go straight back to the kitchen. Thus, the cooks can get started immediately which shortens table turn times and increases how many parties you can seat each day. All that adds up to more revenue, just by reducing how long it takes to run orders to the back of the house."},{"type":"p","text":"The POP also gives your team more flexibility to offer a premiere guest experience. It takes all kinds of payment methods and splits the check, so every party member pays for their meal however works best for them. No matter how they choose to complete the transaction, eatOS POP makes it easy, safe and secure. Our cloud-based system encrypts and stores data so your customers never have to worry."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Stop by booth to see the debut in person!"},{"type":"h2","text":"eatOS Partnerships at RetailNOW"},{"type":"p","text":"Some of our fantastic merchant partners sponsored the RetailNOW show, too. Star Micronics is also attending. Check out their podcast, where you might recognize one of our own eatOS team as a guest!"},{"type":"p","text":"We’re thrilled and honored to be part of a one-of-a-kind industry event as big as this trade show, with so many leaders and experts in attendance. Stop by and say hi, and check out the debut of our new eatOS Point of Purchase too."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant #CloudTechnology"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_b37ce3c78e1046a884d49b2339f4acdb~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-20', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-trends-that-will-define-2021', 'Restaurant Trends that Will Define 2021', 'The foodservice industry spent most of 2020 learning to adapt for COVID-19, but now they’re starting to adjust for what comes next. As customers get used to dining out again, new restaurant trends will overtake what’s...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The foodservice industry spent most of 2020 learning to adapt for COVID-19, but now they’re starting to adjust for what comes next. As customers get used to dining out again, new restaurant trends will overtake what’s currently popular and your restaurant has to be ready to change too."},{"type":"p","text":"Here are five restaurant trends to look out for in 2021."},{"type":"h2","text":"Restaurant Trends on the Rise"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Prioritizing Comfort"},{"type":"p","text":"Six-foot social distance regulations. Mask mandates. Constant sanitization and COVID-19 infections causing temporary shutdowns. Right now, safety concerns reign."},{"type":"p","text":"As normalcy returns, people will seek the comfort and relaxation that they haven’t felt at a restaurant for over a year. Creating a relaxed space for customers to spend time together will be a massive draw moving forward. Warm hospitality goes hand-in-hand with a comfortable seating area to get customers to de-stress and enjoy their time at your restaurant."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Virtual Experiences"},{"type":"p","text":"Most likely, your target base has gotten comfortable online during this pandemic. The world went digital, so why shouldn’t your restaurant follow? Draw in online audiences with whatever your restaurant offers that nobody else can. What sets you apart from the competition? Maybe you’ll team up with famous chefs to share cooking tips with people via video chat. Offer virtual classes where your own back of house teaches a few staple recipes. This is the perfect time to put your creativity to work."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also expand your online services. Start a store with merchandise, gift cards, and meal kits, whatever appeals to your target audience best. New sales avenues can optimize your online presence for as long as you need to prioritize virtual services."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Waste Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Food waste can account for so much of your unnecessary expenses. Although this has always been true, now that COVID-19 has changed the marketplace so thoroughly, it’s time to reassess even if you prioritized waste reduction before."},{"type":"p","text":"Check your sales reports for key insights into how the pandemic has affected inventory and profit. Your average order and ticket sizes have likely changed, as well as the price of ingredients and how long they last before you need to restock. Updating this information reduces unnecessary labor costs and tells you how to appropriately price your own dishes to get a good ROI. For example, you might find that seasonal menus and local ingredients better constrain prices in an unstable market."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Healthy Alternatives"},{"type":"p","text":"Nutrition concerns are on the rise, as consumers expect allergy- and diet-friendly options and favor functional ingredients too. Soy and vegan choices, as well as plant-based alternatives, thrive as customers seek more vitamins, probiotics, and immune-boosting capabilities. Even drinks menus are seeing trends toward healthy options, with low-calorie alternatives, hard seltzer, and hard kombucha gaining popularity this past year."},{"type":"p","text":"A food’s origin story matters. People want sustainably sourced ingredients, local suppliers, and animal and workers’ rights. Stuck at home, they’ve also expanded their palates to try new foods from all over the world. Experimenting with new dishes could pay off while people are feeling adventurous."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Contactless Services"},{"type":"p","text":"Social distance has necessitated touch-free services. Customers crave a safe dining experience whether they choose sit-down or delivery. From curbside pickup services to contactless payment options, touch-free solutions are growing to the point where even dine-in services have contactless alternatives now. With QR codes, guests can scan to pull up a digital menu on their smartphone where they can order can pay from their seats."},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize sanitation and distance as you create new habits in accordance with the changing marketplace. Keep customers engaged and happy to order from you with contactless services. This trend is set to continue long-term so build up your digital marketing and online ordering platforms in preparation to rely on them for a while, even after we move past the pandemic."},{"type":"h2","text":"Following Restaurant Trends"},{"type":"p","text":"Upgrade your restaurant technology so you can grow and change with the times. The best businesses run on smart Point of Sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #CoronavirusPandemic #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantRecovery #Covid19Pandemic #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_cff4e3ec866f4734aeaa7d817258515d~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Growth', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-18', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurants-give-back-does-charity-drive-sales', 'Restaurants Give Back: Does Charity Drive Sales?', 'Money has become a bigger concern for the restaurant industry than ever before, because of COVID-19. Customers are less financially secure, likewise for businesses, and the community as a whole hasn’t fared much better....', '[{"type":"p","text":"Money has become a bigger concern for the restaurant industry than ever before, because of COVID-19. Customers are less financially secure, likewise for businesses, and the community as a whole hasn’t fared much better. When guests do spend money, they want to know it goes to a worthwhile cause. Because of this, as you get more involved with charity, sales will soar."},{"type":"p","text":"Why is that?"},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by RODNAE Productions from Pexels"},{"type":"h2","text":"Customers, Charity, and the Middleman"},{"type":"p","text":"More fundraising organizations have cropped up in response to the pandemic, and a lot of people need help. Spread the word to your audience and they’ll get the resources they need, while customers feel better about where their money goes."},{"type":"p","text":"Given that funds are tight, people look for businesses that share their values. For example, environmentally-focused customers will want to align themselves with green companies. Your restaurant’s charity sets you apart as worthwhile. This boost to your reputation underscores how the company mission connects to your core values. This matters; according to Accenture, a consulting service, in 2018 two-thirds of customers reported that they would rather buy from businesses that share their beliefs. This leads to more customer loyalty which leads to more spending."},{"type":"p","text":"Bring customers and charity together in your restaurant. It fosters goodwill in the community and your reputation will soar."},{"type":"h2","text":"What and How to Donate"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify who your restaurant wants to help. It depends on your community. Perhaps there are a lot of families in need; if so, work directly with outreach organizations that take your leftovers at the end of the day. This has the dual benefit of giving restaurant-quality ingredients to those who wouldn’t otherwise be able to afford it, so they can feed their family healthy meals. Meanwhile, restaurants generate a lot of food waste. Eliminate some by donating your overstock so it goes to good use."},{"type":"p","text":"Alternatively, get food to those in need by hosting food drive events or partnering up with food banks directly. Keep visible collection boxes out so people can drop off cans the next time they visit or offer coupons for every donation to incentivize charity."},{"type":"p","text":"Money goes far for these kinds of organizations, too. Write on each menu that a portion of the check goes to charity, or host fundraisers to donate to third parties that distribute to the needy. People want to help their neighbors, and your restaurant can create avenues to do so."},{"type":"h2","text":"Direct Charity for Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"Don’t rely on third parties. There are things your business can do without help. For example, donate spare PPE to places that still need more, like hospitals or reopening schools. You might also host dinners for hungry community members. Team up with other restaurants in the area to cut down on costs. Open yourself up to donations to help fund these endeavors, too. If you can’t host in person because of the current labor shortage, or for some other reason, consider delivering directly to homeless shelters, schools and other organizations that can handle a gathering."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by cottonbro from Pexels"},{"type":"p","text":"As the pandemic continues, social media remains the most effective way to spread the word about new endeavors. As you become more involved with charity work, use your pages in creative ways, such as hosting polls to see what fundraisers your guests want, or promoting dinner events in advance."},{"type":"p","text":"Togetherness, flexibility and adaptability will get us through the next, tumultuous months. Restaurant recovery will not be easy. Lean on your network to find creative solutions to the ongoing problems plaguing your neighborhood. There’s no better way to show commitment to the community than by lending a helping hand."},{"type":"p","text":"Make sure your charity efforts run smoothly. eatOS offers an all-in-one cloud-based eco-system exclusively for restaurants. From Point of Sale to Contactless Ordering, Pay & Order at Table, Kitchen Display System, Guest Facing Display, Online Ordering APP / Website and Workforce Management there is everything to help a restaurant succeed no matter the size. Click Here to Schedule a demo to learn more about how your restaurant can make a smooth transition into the world of restaurant technology made simple."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #CoronavirusPandemic #PointofSaleforRestaurants #Covid19Pandemic #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_1f83f01f195248e680523c1f757af61b~mv2.jpg', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-14', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('where-are-pos-trends-heading-next', 'Where Are POS Trends Heading Next?', 'Every aspect of the restaurant industry has changed during COVID-19, even its technology. Advanced Point of Sale systems now run restaurants all over the country. Trends indicate that POS will stay on this track for a...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Every aspect of the restaurant industry has changed during COVID-19, even its technology. Advanced Point of Sale systems now run restaurants all over the country. Trends indicate that POS will stay on this track for a long time."},{"type":"p","text":"Here’s what the industry can expect to see out of POS trends."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Mark OFlynn on Unsplash"},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. POS in More Businesses"},{"type":"p","text":"With the pandemic finally ending, more people see the value in upgrading their systems. Previous to COVID-19, restaurants were much warier of new tech. They worried whether their customers and staff could smoothly adapt. They wondered if the cost of investment would ever match ROI. However since the pandemic caused a massive sweep in restaurants digitizing their processes, it’s now status quo for new businesses to open with top-of-the-line equipment from the start."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants aren’t the only businesses in hospitality that noticed these upsides. You’re more likely to see smarter Point of Sales in coffee shops, bars, and all kinds of places besides fine dining. POS capable of more than a standard register is commonplace in a post-pandemic world."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Widening to New Consumers"},{"type":"p","text":"Flexibility has been key this year. Coronavirus regulations shift as swiftly as customer preferences, so the businesses that thrive are the ones that adapt. For many restaurants, that meant turning to entirely new customer touchpoints. Delivery and takeout largely replaced face-time with your guests. Now everyone is comfortable with these channels. Thus some habits will remain long after the world reopens."},{"type":"p","text":"What generates business? Self-service options are extremely popular. Even when people move off the apps to dine-in seating, restaurants can incorporate digitization even there. For example, QR codes enable customers to pull up the menu, order, and pay right from their seats and on their phones. More and more restaurants are also choosing to invest in a Kiosk, especially considering the labor shortage that currently has a stranglehold on businesses. Digitization helps them contend with more foot traffic as things open back up."},{"type":"p","text":"Still, these changes aren’t all good news. They may experience slight delays because they need more regular sanitation, for example. Temperature checks, and collecting info at the door in case of contact tracing, takes a lot of time. Don’t let that deter you though: Restaurants actually benefit from gathering this information. Use it to build out your customer profiles and develop a stronger understanding of your best patrons’ habits and preferences. This will strengthen marketing campaigns and ultimately pull in more money, too!"},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. A POS for the Whole Restaurant"},{"type":"p","text":"As we mentioned above, Point of Sales aren’t just cash registers anymore. Now they do so much more. The POS system powered by eatOS, for example, covers your commercial kitchen, servers, online orders and everywhere else you need to run your business. From tablets that submit orders tableside, to a branded mobile app made just for you, restaurants can streamline their operation from order to checkout."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_e484e7ce260c4c50aadec48d69161dcf~mv2.jpeg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-04-13', 'published');
